{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01P2dXveki5so478t7EhSXGa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Looking at the experiment plan and median tier definition, I'll generate the detailed imagined data.\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claims 需降级但不改方向。Claim 1 从 \"5-10x\" 改为 \"up to Nx in high-heterogeneity regimes\"，\n  强调 regime-dependent。Claim 2 中 HB 的 value proposition 从 \"RMSE reduction\" 转向\n  \"automatic robustness guarantee\"（never-worse-than-global），弱化绝对性能优势。Claim 3 诊断准则\n  从 \"sharp threshold\" 改为 \"useful screening tool with practitioner-chosen operating point\"。\n  K>2 需加 Remark 说明高阶项但非完整理论。PPCI 比较需要 Table 精确列出各场景差异，\n  避免简单正交叙事。补充 robustness analysis（exp-010）展示 graceful degradation。\n  论文仍可投 EMNLP main，但需要更多 empirical depth 补偿理论锐度不足。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Hierarchical Bayesian Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator with partial pooling,\n      compared against MLE/Laplace on full regime sweep (extreme/moderate/homogeneous ×\n      n_expert 100-2000 × K=2,4). MCMC via PyMC NUTS, 4 chains, 1500 warmup, 1000 draws.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- HB vs MLE RMSE (subgroup CATE bias) ---\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n100_K2_extreme: 0.72   # HB RMSE / MLE RMSE ratio — HB wins big at small n\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n250_K2_extreme: 0.88   # advantage narrows\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n500_K2_extreme: 0.95   # marginal at n=500\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n1000_K2_extreme: 0.98  # essentially tied\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n250_K2_moderate: 0.93  # moderate regime — less room to improve\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n250_K2_homogeneous: 0.99  # homogeneous — no benefit, no harm\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n100_K4_extreme: 0.65   # K=4 + small n — HB shines\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n250_K4_extreme: 0.82   # K=4 still benefits more than K=2\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n500_K4_extreme: 0.91\n      # --- Coverage (nominal 95%) ---\n      coverage_hb_n250_K2_extreme: 0.91       # slight undercoverage\n      coverage_hb_n500_K2_extreme: 0.93\n      coverage_hb_n1000_K2_extreme: 0.94\n      coverage_hb_n250_K4_extreme: 0.89       # K=4 worse — more parameters, less data per cell\n      coverage_hb_n500_K4_extreme: 0.91\n      coverage_mle_n250_K2_extreme: 0.83      # MLE substantially undercovered\n      coverage_mle_n500_K2_extreme: 0.89\n      coverage_laplace_n250_K2_extreme: 0.87  # Laplace between MLE and HB\n      # --- MCMC diagnostics ---\n      rhat_max_across_params: 1.003\n      ess_bulk_min: 380\n      ess_tail_min: 220\n      divergences_per_chain: 0\n      mcmc_runtime_seconds_per_mc_rep: 4.2    # ~4s per MCMC fit\n      mle_runtime_seconds_per_mc_rep: 0.02\n      runtime_ratio_hb_vs_mle: 210\n      # --- Never-worse-than-global guarantee ---\n      hb_worse_than_global_fraction: 0.0      # HB never worse than global across all settings\n      hb_worse_than_mle_fraction_n1000: 0.03  # at large n, HB occasionally trivially worse than MLE\n      # --- Total MC runs ---\n      total_mc_reps: 1000\n      se_on_rmse_ratio: 0.008                 # SE of RMSE ratio estimate\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 HB partial pooling 的 value proposition 在 n_expert<150 时显著，n=250 时边际。\n      原因：Dirichlet 先验在小样本时提供正则化，将不稳定的 per-subgroup MLE 估计向全局均值收缩，\n      避免极端的混淆矩阵估计导致的 CATE 校正爆炸。但当 n_expert 足够大（≥500），MLE 本身已稳定，\n      HB 的收缩几乎不改变估计。K=4 下 HB 优势更持久是因为每个 subgroup 分到的样本更少（n/K），\n      收缩效应持续到更大的 n。Coverage 存在轻微 undercoverage（89-93%）而非理论 95%，\n      原因是 posterior variance 未完全捕捉混淆矩阵估计误差向 CATE 校正的非线性传播——\n      delta method 近似 underestimates variance。MCMC 诊断干净（R̂<1.01, ESS>200），\n      但运行时间比 MLE 慢 200x，需在论文中讨论实际部署 trade-off。\n      关键发现：HB 的 \"never worse than global\" 性质在所有 setting 下成立——这是因为\n      partial pooling 在 data-poor 时自动退化为 global estimator，在 data-rich 时退化为 stratified MLE，\n      提供单调改进保证。这成为 median 档下 HB 的核心卖点，替代绝对 RMSE 优势。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T1\"\n        caption: \"HB vs MLE vs Laplace: RMSE ratio and coverage across regimes (K=2)\"\n        columns: [\"regime\", \"n_expert\", \"HB/MLE RMSE\", \"HB Coverage\", \"MLE Coverage\", \"Laplace Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"extreme\", 100, \"0.72 (0.02)\", \"0.90 (0.01)\", \"0.79 (0.02)\", \"0.84 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 250, \"0.88 (0.01)\", \"0.91 (0.01)\", \"0.83 (0.01)\", \"0.87 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 500, \"0.95 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\", \"0.89 (0.01)\", \"0.91 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 1000, \"0.98 (0.01)\", \"0.94 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"moderate\", 250, \"0.93 (0.01)\", \"0.92 (0.01)\", \"0.87 (0.01)\", \"0.89 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"homogeneous\", 250, \"0.99 (0.01)\", \"0.94 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\"]\n      - table_id: \"T2\"\n        caption: \"HB vs MLE: RMSE ratio across regimes (K=4)\"\n        columns: [\"regime\", \"n_expert\", \"HB/MLE RMSE\", \"HB Coverage\", \"MLE Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"extreme\", 100, \"0.65 (0.02)\", \"0.88 (0.01)\", \"0.72 (0.02)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 250, \"0.82 (0.01)\", \"0.89 (0.01)\", \"0.80 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 500, \"0.91 (0.01)\", \"0.91 (0.01)\", \"0.86 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 1000, \"0.97 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\", \"0.91 (0.01)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: RMSE ratio (HB/MLE) vs n_expert curves, separate lines for K=2 and K=4, shaded 95% CI bands. Shows HB advantage decaying toward 1.0 as n grows, with K=4 curve consistently below K=2.\"\n      - \"Fig: Coverage vs n_expert, three estimators (HB/MLE/Laplace), horizontal dashed line at 0.95. Shows all undercovering but HB closest to nominal.\"\n    analysis: >\n      HB 的核心价值不在绝对 RMSE 优势（n=250 时仅 12% improvement for K=2），而在两个性质：\n      (1) never-worse-than-global 保证——在 homogeneous regime 下自动收缩回 global，无需 practitioner\n      判断何时该 stratify；(2) K=4 下优势显著持久——实际应用中 subgroup 数常 >2。\n      Undercoverage 问题（88-93% vs nominal 95%）需在论文中诊断：主要原因是 confusion matrix\n      uncertainty 通过矩阵求逆向 CATE 传播时的非线性效应被 delta-method 低估。建议加 Remark\n      说明并推荐 posterior predictive check 作为实践中的 calibration 工具。\n      Runtime 210x overhead 在 MC simulation 中累积严重（4.2s × 1000 reps = 70 min per setting），\n      但实际应用只需 fit 一次，4s 完全可接受。\n\n  - name: \"Bias Bound Verification (K=2 and K=4)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      Derive analytic bias formula bias ∝ Δπ×Δτ for K=2, verify empirically on systematic\n      parameter grid, extend to K=4 with sum-of-products form, assess R² of analytic\n      prediction vs MC simulation.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- K=2 bias formula verification ---\n      r_squared_K2_analytic_vs_mc: 0.89       # good but not perfect fit\n      r_squared_K2_with_intercept: 0.91       # allowing intercept slightly improves\n      bias_bound_tightness_ratio_K2_median: 1.15  # analytic bound / MC bias — slightly loose\n      bias_bound_tightness_ratio_K2_p90: 1.45     # tail cases where bound is loose\n      # --- K=4 extension ---\n      r_squared_K4_sum_of_products: 0.76      # K=4 substantially worse with simple formula\n      r_squared_K4_with_interaction_terms: 0.84  # adding pairwise interactions helps\n      r_squared_K4_full_model: 0.88           # with all higher-order terms, recovers K=2 quality\n      # --- \"Debiasing can hurt\" proposition ---\n      bias_amplification_extreme_regime: 4.2   # global correction / no correction bias ratio\n      bias_amplification_moderate_regime: 2.3\n      bias_amplification_homogeneous_regime: 1.05  # near 1 — global doesn't hurt when homogeneous\n      # --- Parameter grid coverage ---\n      n_grid_points_delta_pi: 10              # Δπ from 0.02 to 0.25\n      n_grid_points_delta_tau: 10             # Δτ from 0.05 to 0.50\n      n_mc_reps_per_point: 1000\n      se_on_bias_ratio: 0.05\n      # --- Specific constructive example (two-subgroup) ---\n      constructive_example_subgroup1_bias_global: 0.18    # over-correction\n      constructive_example_subgroup2_bias_global: -0.14   # under-correction\n      constructive_example_aggregate_looks_ok: true        # aggregate bias ~0.02, masks subgroup issue\n      constructive_example_subgroup1_bias_nocorrection: 0.04\n      constructive_example_subgroup2_bias_nocorrection: -0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 K=2 的 R²≥0.85 但非 0.95+，因为 Δπ×Δτ 是一阶近似——忽略了混淆矩阵\n      off-diagonal 的二阶交互以及样本量有限时的随机波动。在 Δπ 或 Δτ 极端时（>0.15 或 >0.35），\n      non-linear terms 变得 non-negligible，拖低整体 R²。R²=0.89 意味着 Δπ×Δτ 捕捉了 89%\n      的 systematic variation——足够作为诊断工具的理论基础，但需要在论文中明确标注 \"first-order\n      approximation\" 而非 \"exact characterization\"。\n\n      K=4 下 R² 显著下降至 0.76 是因为 K=4 有 C(4,2)=6 个 subgroup pair 的交互，\n      简单 sum-of-products Σ(Δπ_k × Δτ_k) 忽略了 cross-subgroup misclassification routing\n      （subgroup A 的样本被误分到 subgroup B 而非 C 的具体 pattern 不被 marginal Δπ 捕捉）。\n      加入 pairwise interaction terms 后恢复到 0.84，说明 K>2 的理论需要更精细的建模。\n      这支持论文中加 Remark 而非完整 K>2 定理。\n\n      Bias amplification 在 extreme regime 达到 4.2x（而非 framing 中的 5-10x）——\n      这是因为 \"5-10x\" 需要非常极端的参数组合（Δπ>0.15 且 Δτ>0.3），median 档下\n      semi-synthetic 数据中的 LLM 误分类异质性较温和，实际 Δπ 多在 0.05-0.12 范围。\n      论文需将 headline 从 \"5-10x\" 改为 \"up to 4-5x in high-heterogeneity regimes\"。\n\n      Constructive two-subgroup example 的关键 insight：aggregate bias 接近 0（0.02），\n      因为 over-correction 和 under-correction 部分抵消。这意味着仅看 aggregate metrics\n      的研究者会认为 global correction 工作良好，而实际 subgroup-level bias 高达 0.18。\n      这是 paper 的核心 narrative hook。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T3\"\n        caption: \"Analytic bias bound R² by K and model specification\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"Model\", \"R²\", \"Bound tightness (median)\", \"Bound tightness (90th pct)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [2, \"Δπ×Δτ (no intercept)\", \"0.89\", \"1.15\", \"1.45\"]\n          - [2, \"Δπ×Δτ (with intercept)\", \"0.91\", \"1.12\", \"1.38\"]\n          - [4, \"Σ(Δπ_k×Δτ_k)\", \"0.76\", \"1.32\", \"1.85\"]\n          - [4, \"+ pairwise interactions\", \"0.84\", \"1.20\", \"1.55\"]\n          - [4, \"+ all higher-order\", \"0.88\", \"1.14\", \"1.42\"]\n      - table_id: \"T4\"\n        caption: \"Bias amplification factor (global correction / no correction) by regime\"\n        columns: [\"regime\", \"Δπ range\", \"Δτ range\", \"amplification (mean ± SE)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"extreme\", \"0.10-0.25\", \"0.20-0.50\", \"4.2 ± 0.3\"]\n          - [\"moderate\", \"0.05-0.12\", \"0.10-0.25\", \"2.3 ± 0.2\"]\n          - [\"mild\", \"0.02-0.05\", \"0.05-0.12\", \"1.4 ± 0.1\"]\n          - [\"homogeneous\", \"< 0.02\", \"any\", \"1.05 ± 0.05\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Bias amplification heatmap — x-axis Δπ (0.02-0.25), y-axis Δτ (0.05-0.50), color = global/no-correction bias ratio. Diagonal contour lines show iso-amplification. Clear gradient from bottom-left (≈1) to top-right (≈5). Key for paper Figure 2.\"\n      - \"Fig: Analytic prediction vs MC bias scatter plot, K=2 and K=4 side by side. K=2 tightly clustered around 45° line; K=4 shows more dispersion, especially at high bias values.\"\n      - \"Fig: Constructive two-subgroup example bar chart — subgroup 1 and 2 bias under no-correction, global correction, and EC-HTE. Shows global correction flipping sign of bias for subgroup 1.\"\n    analysis: >\n      R²=0.89 (K=2) 足够支撑 diagnostic criterion 但需要 honest framing：论文应写\n      \"the Δπ×Δτ product explains ~90% of bias variance in the K=2 setting\"\n      而非 \"bias is exactly proportional to Δπ×Δτ\"。K=4 的 R²=0.76 是写 Remark 而非 Theorem\n      的理由——可以说 \"empirically the sum-of-products form captures the dominant variation\n      but cross-subgroup misclassification routing introduces additional structure not\n      captured by marginal heterogeneity measures\"。这反而可以作为 future work 的自然 hook。\n      Bias amplification 4.2x（非 7.8x）意味着 headline 需要调整。可以在 abstract 中写\n      \"up to 4x in realistic settings\"，在 appendix 中展示极端参数下理论上可达更高倍数。\n\n  - name: \"Semi-Synthetic Political Science Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      Real political-science tweet corpus with injected CATE heterogeneity structure,\n      annotated by GPT-4.1 and Qwen3-235B-A22B. Measure subgroup-specific misclassification\n      rates, apply EC-HTE vs baselines (no correction, global correction, MLE stratified,\n      HB stratified).\n    expected_results:\n      # --- LLM annotation quality ---\n      gpt4_overall_accuracy: 0.82\n      gpt4_subgroup_accuracy_range: [0.75, 0.88]   # max/min ratio ~1.17\n      gpt4_misclass_heterogeneity_delta_pi_max: 0.09\n      qwen3_overall_accuracy: 0.76\n      qwen3_subgroup_accuracy_range: [0.67, 0.83]   # max/min ratio ~1.24\n      qwen3_misclass_heterogeneity_delta_pi_max: 0.13\n      # --- CATE bias results (primary) ---\n      # subgroup CATE RMSE across methods — n_expert=500, K=2\n      rmse_no_correction: 0.145\n      rmse_global_correction: 0.198           # global makes it worse\n      rmse_mle_stratified: 0.078\n      rmse_hb_stratified: 0.072               # HB marginally better than MLE at n=500\n      rmse_oracle_stratified: 0.035           # oracle = true confusion matrices\n      # --- Bias amplification ---\n      bias_amplification_gpt4: 2.8            # global/no-correction on GPT-4.1 annotations\n      bias_amplification_qwen3: 3.6           # worse for noisier annotator\n      # --- EC-HTE subgroup bias reduction vs global ---\n      ec_hte_bias_reduction_vs_global_gpt4: 0.72   # EC-HTE subgroup bias / global subgroup bias\n      ec_hte_bias_reduction_vs_global_qwen3: 0.65\n      # --- Coverage ---\n      coverage_hb_gpt4_n500: 0.91\n      coverage_hb_qwen3_n500: 0.89\n      coverage_global_gpt4_n500: 0.78\n      # --- Sample sizes ---\n      n_tweets_total: 12000\n      n_expert_labels: 500\n      n_subgroups: 2\n      # --- Causal estimator ---\n      cate_estimator: \"difference-in-means within strata\"\n      injected_cate_subgroup1: 0.15\n      injected_cate_subgroup2: 0.35\n      injected_delta_tau: 0.20\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 LLM 误分类异质性存在但较温和（max/min accuracy ratio 1.17-1.24），\n      这是因为现代 LLMs（GPT-4.1, Qwen3）的分类能力已较强，subgroup 间的 accuracy 差异\n      主要来自 label ambiguity 和 subgroup-specific language patterns，而非系统性能力差异。\n      GPT-4.1 的 Δπ_max=0.09 对应于 bias amplification 2.8x——低于 framing 中的 5-10x\n      但仍然实质性。Qwen3 因整体质量更低，Δπ_max=0.13，amplification 达到 3.6x。\n\n      HB vs MLE 在 n_expert=500 时仅有 marginal improvement（0.072 vs 0.078 RMSE）——\n      这与 exp-001 的发现一致：n=500/K=2=250 per subgroup，已足够 MLE 稳定。\n      论文需要在此处强调 HB 的 robustness guarantee 而非 RMSE improvement。\n\n      EC-HTE bias reduction vs global 在 0.65-0.72 范围——显著但非 dramatic。这意味着\n      EC-HTE 将 global correction 的 subgroup bias 减少了 28-35%，而非消除。残余 bias\n      来自有限 expert labels 下混淆矩阵估计的噪声（非系统性的）。\n\n      Coverage 89-91% 而非 95% 延续了 exp-001 的 undercoverage pattern。在 semi-synthetic\n      setting 中这更显著因为 injected CATE structure 的复杂性超过了纯 synthetic 的简单设定。\n\n      Qwen3 的 bias amplification (3.6x) > GPT-4.1 (2.8x) 提供了一个自然的 narrative：\n      \"lower-quality annotators produce more heterogeneous errors, making the bias mechanism\n      more severe — precisely the setting where EC-HTE is most needed\"。这是论文的关键 empirical\n      point。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T5\"\n        caption: \"Semi-synthetic benchmark: subgroup CATE estimation across methods (K=2, n_expert=500)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Subgroup 1 Bias\", \"Subgroup 2 Bias\", \"RMSE\", \"Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"No correction\", \"0.08 (0.02)\", \"-0.11 (0.02)\", \"0.145 (0.008)\", \"0.85 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"Global correction\", \"-0.14 (0.03)\", \"0.15 (0.03)\", \"0.198 (0.012)\", \"0.78 (0.02)\"]\n          - [\"MLE stratified\", \"0.02 (0.03)\", \"-0.03 (0.03)\", \"0.078 (0.010)\", \"0.87 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"HB stratified (EC-HTE)\", \"0.01 (0.02)\", \"-0.02 (0.02)\", \"0.072 (0.008)\", \"0.91 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"Oracle stratified\", \"0.00 (0.01)\", \"0.00 (0.01)\", \"0.035 (0.004)\", \"0.95 (0.01)\"]\n      - table_id: \"T6\"\n        caption: \"LLM annotation quality by subgroup\"\n        columns: [\"LLM\", \"Overall Acc\", \"Subgroup 1 Acc\", \"Subgroup 2 Acc\", \"Δπ_max\", \"Bias Amplification\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4.1\", \"0.82\", \"0.88\", \"0.75\", \"0.09\", \"2.8\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-235B\", \"0.76\", \"0.83\", \"0.67\", \"0.13\", \"3.6\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Subgroup bias bar chart — 4 methods × 2 subgroups, showing sign flip under global correction. Key paper Figure 3.\"\n      - \"Fig: Bias amplification scatter — x-axis Δπ (from both LLMs), y-axis amplification factor, with analytic prediction line from exp-002 overlaid. Shows semi-synthetic points fall near analytic prediction.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Semi-synthetic 结果与 synthetic (exp-001/002) 的一致性是关键：analytic prediction (exp-002)\n      预测 Δπ=0.09 时 amplification ~2.5-3x，实际 GPT-4.1 得到 2.8x，验证了理论。\n      但 LLM 误分类异质性较温和（ratio 1.17-1.24 vs 需要 >1.5 才能产生 dramatic effects），\n      这是 median 档的核心特征——效应存在但需要选择性展示 regime。论文策略：用 Qwen3（更大异质性）\n      作为 primary showcase，GPT-4.1 作为 \"even with a good annotator, the effect exists\" 的补充。\n      Oracle RMSE (0.035) vs EC-HTE (0.072) 的 gap 说明混淆矩阵估计的 noise floor 是实际瓶颈，\n      不是方法本身的系统偏差——这支持 \"more expert labels always help\" 的 message。\n\n  - name: \"Real-Data Validation (Ashwin et al.)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Apply EC-HTE to Ashwin et al. (2025) Rohingya refugee interview dataset where\n      LLM annotation errors correlate with refugee status, gender, education.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Dataset characteristics ---\n      n_interviews: 1800\n      n_expert_coded: 400                      # subset with expert labels\n      annotation_categories: 5                 # trauma, resilience, agency, blame, neutral\n      subgroups_by: \"refugee_status × gender\"  # 2×2 = 4 cells\n      # --- LLM annotation heterogeneity ---\n      gpt4_overall_accuracy_5class: 0.68\n      gpt4_accuracy_range_by_subgroup: [0.58, 0.76]  # substantial heterogeneity\n      gpt4_delta_pi_max: 0.14\n      # --- CATE results (treatment = interview framing) ---\n      cate_global_correction_bias_worst_subgroup: 0.22\n      cate_no_correction_bias_worst_subgroup: 0.09\n      cate_echte_bias_worst_subgroup: 0.05\n      bias_amplification_global: 3.1\n      # --- But real data is messy ---\n      cate_uncertainty_wide: true               # CIs are wide due to small n per cell\n      echte_vs_mle_difference_significant: false # p=0.18 for RMSE difference\n      coverage_hb: 0.90\n      coverage_global: 0.74\n      # --- Qualitative findings ---\n      worst_subgroup: \"female refugees\"         # highest misclassification, highest CATE\n      best_subgroup: \"male host community\"      # lowest misclassification\n      bias_direction_global: \"over-correction of male host community, under-correction of female refugees\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Real data 验证在 median 档下呈现 \"directionally correct but noisy\" 的模式。\n      Ashwin et al. 数据的 5-class 分类比 binary 更难，GPT-4.1 overall accuracy 仅 0.68，\n      且 refugee status × gender 产生的 subgroup 异质性（0.58-0.76）比 semi-synthetic 更大——\n      这是因为 LLM 在处理 trauma-related narratives 时，对女性难民的文化特定表达识别率更低。\n\n      Bias amplification 3.1x 与 semi-synthetic 一致，但因为 real data 的 treatment effect\n      本身 uncertainty 更大（不是 injected 的），EC-HTE vs MLE 的差异在统计上不显著（p=0.18）。\n      这是 median 档的典型 real-data 结果：方向正确但 power 不足以宣称显著优势。\n\n      论文策略：将 real-data 作为 \"proof of concept\" 而非 \"primary evidence\"，\n      强调 bias mechanism 在 real data 中确实存在（global correction 的 worst-subgroup bias\n      0.22 vs no-correction 的 0.09），EC-HTE 改善方向正确（0.05），但承认 sample size\n      限制了 statistical power。Coverage 差异（0.90 vs 0.74）在 real data 中尤其有意义——\n      global correction 的 CI 严重 miscalibrated。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T7\"\n        caption: \"Ashwin et al. real-data: worst-subgroup CATE bias by method\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Worst subgroup bias\", \"Mean abs bias\", \"Coverage\", \"CI width\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"No correction\", \"0.09\", \"0.06\", \"0.86\", \"0.28\"]\n          - [\"Global correction\", \"0.22\", \"0.14\", \"0.74\", \"0.25\"]\n          - [\"MLE stratified\", \"0.07\", \"0.05\", \"0.83\", \"0.35\"]\n          - [\"HB stratified (EC-HTE)\", \"0.05\", \"0.03\", \"0.90\", \"0.32\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Heatmap of LLM accuracy by subgroup (refugee_status × gender × annotation_category). Shows clear pattern of lower accuracy for female refugees on trauma/agency categories.\"\n      - \"Fig: CATE estimates ± CI by subgroup, 4 methods side by side. Shows global correction distorting relative ordering of subgroup effects.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Real data 中最有价值的发现是 bias 的 substantive interpretation：global correction\n      系统性低估 female refugees 的 treatment effect 同时高估 male host community——\n      这有直接的 policy relevance（错误的 subgroup 优先级排序）。即使 EC-HTE 的 statistical\n      improvement 边际，correcting the direction of subgroup ranking 具有实际意义。\n      论文应强调这个 qualitative finding 而非纠结 p-value。数据集 4 个 subgroup × 400 expert\n      labels 意味着每个 cell ~100 个 labels，处于 HB 优势最明显的 regime（与 exp-001 一致）。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Criterion Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Compute misclass_heterogeneity × CATE_heterogeneity product from pilot data,\n      evaluate as binary classifier for \"global correction is harmful\". ROC analysis.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Diagnostic performance ---\n      diagnostic_auc: 0.82                     # moderate, not sharp\n      diagnostic_auc_ci_95: [0.77, 0.87]\n      # --- Operating point analysis ---\n      threshold_high_sensitivity: 0.015        # catches 90% of harmful cases\n      sensitivity_at_high_threshold: 0.90\n      specificity_at_high_threshold: 0.55      # many false alarms\n      threshold_balanced: 0.035                # balanced operating point\n      sensitivity_at_balanced: 0.75\n      specificity_at_balanced: 0.72\n      threshold_high_specificity: 0.065        # few false alarms\n      sensitivity_at_high_specificity: 0.55\n      specificity_at_high_specificity: 0.90\n      # --- Where the gray zone is ---\n      gray_zone_product_range: [0.02, 0.06]    # ambiguous zone\n      fraction_settings_in_gray_zone: 0.35     # 35% of settings fall here\n      # --- Comparison to simpler diagnostics ---\n      auc_delta_pi_only: 0.73                  # misclass heterogeneity alone\n      auc_delta_tau_only: 0.65                 # CATE heterogeneity alone\n      auc_product_advantage_over_best_single: 0.09  # product adds 9 AUC points\n      # --- From different data sources ---\n      auc_using_synthetic_threshold_on_semisynthetic: 0.79  # slight degradation on transfer\n      auc_on_real_data_ashwin: 0.78            # further degradation on real\n    result_rationale: >\n      AUC=0.82 而非 >0.90 的原因：diagnostic product Δπ×Δτ 是 bias 的一阶近似（exp-002\n      已展示 R²=0.89），但将 continuous bias magnitude 转为 binary \"harmful/not harmful\"\n      引入了 threshold-dependent noise——接近 boundary 的 cases 本质上模糊。此外，\n      \"harmful\" 的定义本身有 arbitrariness（global bias > 1.5x no-correction? 2x? depends on\n      acceptable bias level），不同的 ground truth definition 改变 AUC ±0.03。\n\n      35% 的 settings 落在 gray zone 是 median 档的核心特征——实际数据中 Δπ 和 Δτ\n      往往不极端，导致大量 \"depends on your tolerance\" cases。这迫使论文从 \"sharp threshold\"\n      转向 \"practitioner-chosen operating point\" 的 framing。\n\n      Product 比单一 metric 强 9 AUC points（0.82 vs 0.73），证明了两个维度的交互信息——\n      但不是 dramatic improvement。Δπ alone AUC=0.73 说明即使只看误分类异质性也有一定诊断力。\n\n      Transfer performance 从 synthetic (AUC=0.82) 到 semi-synthetic (0.79) 到 real (0.78)\n      呈现 graceful degradation——阈值具有一定 portability 但非 universal。\n      论文建议 practitioners 用小规模 pilot study 校准阈值。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T8\"\n        caption: \"Diagnostic criterion ROC operating points\"\n        columns: [\"Operating Point\", \"Δπ×Δτ threshold\", \"Sensitivity\", \"Specificity\", \"F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"High sensitivity\", \"0.015\", \"0.90\", \"0.55\", \"0.68\"]\n          - [\"Balanced\", \"0.035\", \"0.75\", \"0.72\", \"0.73\"]\n          - [\"High specificity\", \"0.065\", \"0.55\", \"0.90\", \"0.67\"]\n      - table_id: \"T9\"\n        caption: \"Diagnostic AUC comparison across metrics and data sources\"\n        columns: [\"Diagnostic\", \"Synthetic AUC\", \"Semi-synthetic AUC\", \"Real data AUC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Δπ×Δτ product\", \"0.82\", \"0.79\", \"0.78\"]\n          - [\"Δπ only\", \"0.73\", \"0.71\", \"0.70\"]\n          - [\"Δτ only\", \"0.65\", \"0.64\", \"0.62\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: ROC curve with three operating points marked. Gray shaded area shows the region of Δπ×Δτ ∈ [0.02, 0.06] where the diagnostic is ambiguous. Key paper Figure 4.\"\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot of Δπ×Δτ product vs actual bias amplification factor, colored by data source (synthetic/semi-synthetic/real). Shows positive correlation but substantial scatter in the gray zone.\"\n    analysis: >\n      AUC=0.82 的 diagnostic 定位为 \"useful screening tool\" 而非 \"sharp threshold\"。\n      论文 framing：先计算 Δπ×Δτ 作为 pre-analysis step；若 product < 0.015，global correction\n      likely safe（false negative rate ~10%）；若 > 0.065，strongly recommend stratified\n      correction；中间地带需 domain knowledge。这比 \"compute this number, if >X use EC-HTE\"\n      的 sharp rule 更 honest，也更 useful（给 practitioner 决策权而非 black box）。\n      35% gray zone fraction 是主要 limitation，需在论文中 explicitly discuss。\n\n  - name: \"Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Systematic sweep n_expert ∈ {50, 100, 250, 500, 1000, 2000} × K ∈ {2, 4, 8}.\n      Find crossover where EC-HTE outperforms global. Validate HB value at small n.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Crossover points (EC-HTE RMSE < Global RMSE) ---\n      crossover_n_K2_extreme: 180              # need ~180 expert labels for K=2 extreme\n      crossover_n_K2_moderate: 350             # moderate regime needs more\n      crossover_n_K4_extreme: 320              # K=4 needs more total (but less per subgroup)\n      crossover_n_K4_moderate: 480\n      crossover_n_K8_extreme: 600              # K=8 pushes crossover high\n      crossover_n_K8_moderate: \">1000\"         # may not cross within budget\n      # --- HB vs MLE at crossover ---\n      hb_advantage_at_crossover_K2: 0.15       # 15% RMSE improvement over MLE at crossover\n      hb_advantage_at_crossover_K4: 0.22       # HB more valuable at crossover for K=4\n      hb_advantage_at_crossover_K8: 0.28       # and even more for K=8\n      # --- Budget efficiency ---\n      rmse_hb_n50_K2: 0.185                    # very noisy but still directionally helpful\n      rmse_global_n50_K2: 0.210                # global already harmful\n      rmse_hb_n2000_K2: 0.042                  # close to oracle\n      rmse_oracle_K2: 0.035\n      # --- HB \"never worse than global\" ---\n      hb_worse_than_global_any_setting: false   # confirmed across all n×K\n      mle_worse_than_global_at_n50_K4: true     # MLE can be worse at very small n, large K\n      mle_worse_than_global_at_n50_K8: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Crossover point 在 250-500 范围（取决于 K 和 regime severity）而非更低，\n      因为 stratified correction 需要每个 subgroup 有足够 expert labels 来估计 confusion matrix——\n      at minimum ~30-50 per subgroup for stable estimates。K=2 时 n=180 意味着 ~90 per subgroup，\n      刚好够。K=8 时 n=600 意味着 ~75 per subgroup，也是 marginal。\n\n      HB 的优势在 crossover 附近最大（15-28%），因为这正是 MLE 估计开始不稳定的区域——\n      少几个 labels MLE 完全不可用，多几个 MLE 已经稳定，HB 的 partial pooling 正好填补\n      这个 transition zone。K 越大 transition zone 越宽（每个 subgroup 样本更少），\n      所以 HB 优势越持久。\n\n      K=8 + moderate regime 下 crossover 可能超过 n=1000——这是实际限制，论文需 honestly\n      discuss：EC-HTE 在 K>4 时可能需要不切实际的 expert budget，除非 regime 足够 extreme。\n      这支持 \"use diagnostic criterion first, then decide K granularity\" 的 practical workflow。\n\n      MLE 在 n=50, K≥4 时反而比 global 更差——混淆矩阵估计太噪导致 correction 发散。\n      HB 通过收缩避免了这个问题，证明了 \"never worse than global\" 的 practical value。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T10\"\n        caption: \"Crossover expert budget by K and regime\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"Regime\", \"Crossover n\", \"HB RMSE advantage at crossover\"]\n        rows:\n          - [2, \"extreme\", 180, \"15%\"]\n          - [2, \"moderate\", 350, \"10%\"]\n          - [4, \"extreme\", 320, \"22%\"]\n          - [4, \"moderate\", 480, \"16%\"]\n          - [8, \"extreme\", 600, \"28%\"]\n          - [8, \"moderate\", \">1000\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: RMSE vs n_expert curves, separate panels for K=2,4,8. Three lines per panel: global (flat, high), MLE stratified (decreasing, noisy at small n), HB stratified (decreasing, smooth). Vertical dashed line at crossover point. Key paper Figure 5.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Budget sensitivity 是论文实际建议的基础。Key message：对于典型 NLP-CSS study（K=2-4 subgroups，\n      moderate heterogeneity），250-500 expert labels 是 EC-HTE 的 minimum viable budget。\n      这与 expert annotation 的现实成本兼容（500 labels × $2/label = $1000，typical research budget）。\n      K=8 的高 crossover 是 honest limitation——如果 subgroup structure 太细，需要 unrealistic budget\n      或者 collapse subgroups（HB 自动做的 partial pooling 本质上是 soft collapsing）。\n\n  - name: \"PPCI Baseline Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      Head-to-head comparison with PPCI (Sui et al., 2026) on covariate-side vs outcome-side\n      error. Theoretical discussion of composition. If feasible, combined correction experiment.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Scenario A: Covariate-side error only (EC-HTE's home turf) ---\n      echte_bias_cov_error_only: 0.04\n      ppci_bias_cov_error_only: 0.16           # PPCI doesn't address covariate error\n      global_bias_cov_error_only: 0.19\n      # --- Scenario B: Outcome-side error only (PPCI's home turf) ---\n      echte_bias_outcome_error_only: 0.14      # EC-HTE doesn't address outcome error\n      ppci_bias_outcome_error_only: 0.05\n      global_bias_outcome_error_only: 0.15\n      # --- Scenario C: Both errors present ---\n      echte_bias_both_errors: 0.13\n      ppci_bias_both_errors: 0.15\n      global_bias_both_errors: 0.24\n      combined_echte_ppci_bias: 0.08            # sequential application helps\n      # --- But PPCI partially helps on covariate error in some settings ---\n      ppci_bias_cov_error_high_correlation: 0.11  # when covariate error correlates with outcome\n      ppci_partial_effectiveness_on_cov_error: true\n      # --- Coverage ---\n      coverage_echte_cov_only: 0.91\n      coverage_ppci_cov_only: 0.80\n      coverage_ppci_outcome_only: 0.93\n      coverage_echte_outcome_only: 0.82\n      coverage_combined_both: 0.88\n      # --- PPCI implementation details ---\n      ppci_kernel_bandwidth: \"Silverman rule\"\n      ppci_convergence_rate: \"n^{-2/5} for d=1\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 PPCI 比较的关键 nuance：PPCI 在纯 covariate error setting 下并非完全无效\n      （bias 0.16 vs global 0.19），因为当 covariate error 与 outcome 有相关性时，\n      PPCI 的 kernel localization 间接捕捉了一部分 covariate-side heterogeneity。\n      这破坏了 \"完全正交\" 的简单叙事，需要 table 精确列出每个场景。\n\n      具体原因：PPCI 通过 kernel smoothing 估计 conditional expectation E[Y|X]，\n      当 X 的 misclassification 与 Y 的 noise 结构相关时，PPCI 的 correction 会 \"accidentally\"\n      部分校正 covariate error 的影响。这在 high correlation setting 下更明显（bias 0.11 vs 0.16）。\n      但 EC-HTE 仍然显著更优（0.04 vs 0.11），因为它直接 targets covariate error。\n\n      Combined application（先 EC-HTE 校正 covariate error，再 PPCI 校正 outcome error）\n      在 both-errors 场景下达到 bias 0.08——优于任一单独方法（0.13 和 0.15）。\n      但 coverage 降到 0.88，因为两步校正的 uncertainty 叠加。\n      论文可以讨论 composition 作为 future direction，但 median 档下证据不足以作为主要 claim。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T11\"\n        caption: \"EC-HTE vs PPCI: head-to-head by error type (K=2, n_expert=500)\"\n        columns: [\"Error Type\", \"No Correction\", \"Global\", \"EC-HTE\", \"PPCI\", \"EC-HTE+PPCI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Covariate only\", \"0.12\", \"0.19\", \"0.04\", \"0.16\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Covariate (high corr w/ outcome)\", \"0.12\", \"0.19\", \"0.04\", \"0.11\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Outcome only\", \"0.13\", \"0.15\", \"0.14\", \"0.05\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Both\", \"0.18\", \"0.24\", \"0.13\", \"0.15\", \"0.08\"]\n      - table_id: \"T12\"\n        caption: \"Coverage comparison by error type and method\"\n        columns: [\"Error Type\", \"EC-HTE\", \"PPCI\", \"EC-HTE+PPCI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Covariate only\", \"0.91\", \"0.80\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Outcome only\", \"0.82\", \"0.93\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Both\", \"0.85\", \"0.83\", \"0.88\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 2×2 panel showing bias by method across 4 error scenarios. Highlights that each method excels on its target error type, with partial overlap in high-correlation settings.\"\n    analysis: >\n      PPCI 比较的 takeaway 需要 nuance：不是 \"orthogonal problems, use EC-HTE for covariate error\n      and PPCI for outcome error\"，而是 \"EC-HTE strongly dominates on covariate error;\n      PPCI partially helps on covariate error in correlated settings but EC-HTE is 3-4x better;\n      PPCI strongly dominates on outcome error; composition is promising but needs more work\"。\n      论文 Table 11 是关键——需要 reviewers 看到所有场景而非 cherry-picked 对比。\n      特别要 preempt reviewer 质疑 \"PPCI already partially handles this\"：\n      用 high-correlation scenario 的 0.11 vs 0.04 说明 \"partial ≠ adequate\"。\n\n  - name: \"Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4.1 vs Qwen3-235B-A22B vs Claude Sonnet 4.6: measure misclassification heterogeneity\n      patterns, show EC-HTE benefit varies by LLM quality.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Per-LLM quality ---\n      gpt4_accuracy: 0.82\n      gpt4_delta_pi_max: 0.09\n      gpt4_bias_amplification: 2.8\n      qwen3_accuracy: 0.76\n      qwen3_delta_pi_max: 0.13\n      qwen3_bias_amplification: 3.6\n      claude_sonnet_accuracy: 0.79\n      claude_sonnet_delta_pi_max: 0.11\n      claude_sonnet_bias_amplification: 3.1\n      # --- EC-HTE benefit by LLM ---\n      echte_rmse_improvement_gpt4: 0.08        # modest improvement for best LLM\n      echte_rmse_improvement_claude: 0.11\n      echte_rmse_improvement_qwen3: 0.15       # largest improvement for noisiest LLM\n      # --- Correlation between LLM quality and EC-HTE benefit ---\n      correlation_accuracy_vs_echte_benefit: -0.92  # better LLM → less EC-HTE benefit\n      correlation_delta_pi_vs_echte_benefit: 0.88   # more heterogeneous → more benefit\n      # --- Ensemble analysis ---\n      ensemble_majority_vote_accuracy: 0.85\n      ensemble_delta_pi_max: 0.07              # ensemble reduces heterogeneity\n      ensemble_bias_amplification: 2.1         # but doesn't eliminate it\n    result_rationale: >\n      三个 LLM 的 accuracy 排序 GPT-4.1 > Claude Sonnet > Qwen3 反映了模型能力梯度。\n      关键发现是 Δπ（误分类异质性）与 overall accuracy 的关系并非单调——取决于每个 LLM\n      在哪些 subgroup 上 struggle。Claude Sonnet 的 accuracy 介于两者之间，但 Δπ=0.11\n      说明它的 errors 有不同的 subgroup pattern。\n\n      EC-HTE benefit 与 LLM quality 的高负相关（-0.92）是预期的：worse LLM → more heterogeneous\n      errors → more room for stratified correction to help。这支持 \"EC-HTE as insurance policy\"\n      的 narrative——特别是在使用 cheaper/faster 但 noisier LLMs 时。\n\n      Ensemble 分析显示 majority vote 提高 accuracy（0.85）但不消除 heterogeneity（Δπ=0.07，\n      amplification 2.1x），说明 \"just use ensemble\" 不是 EC-HTE 的替代品。\n      但 ensemble + EC-HTE 的 marginal benefit 可能很小，这是 honest limitation。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T13\"\n        caption: \"LLM annotator comparison: quality, heterogeneity, and EC-HTE benefit\"\n        columns: [\"LLM\", \"Accuracy\", \"Δπ_max\", \"Bias Amplification\", \"EC-HTE RMSE Gain\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4.1\", \"0.82\", \"0.09\", \"2.8\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"Claude Sonnet 4.6\", \"0.79\", \"0.11\", \"3.1\", \"0.11\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-235B\", \"0.76\", \"0.13\", \"3.6\", \"0.15\"]\n          - [\"Majority Vote Ensemble\", \"0.85\", \"0.07\", \"2.1\", \"0.05\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot of Δπ_max vs EC-HTE RMSE improvement, one point per LLM + ensemble. Clear positive trend. Could go to appendix.\"\n    analysis: >\n      P1 实验，适合 appendix。核心 message 简洁：EC-HTE 对 noisier annotators 更有价值。\n      Ensemble 不替代 EC-HTE 因为不消除 heterogeneity。三个 LLM 的 heterogeneity pattern\n      不同（different subgroups are hard for different LLMs），说明 one-size-fits-all\n      correction 本质不可行。\n\n  - name: \"Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      CATE-weighted adaptive allocation vs uniform vs uncertainty-only allocation.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Allocation strategies at n_expert=250 ---\n      rmse_uniform_allocation: 0.082\n      rmse_uncertainty_allocation: 0.075       # allocate more to high-uncertainty subgroups\n      rmse_cate_weighted_allocation: 0.071     # allocate more to high-CATE × high-error\n      rmse_oracle_allocation: 0.065\n      # --- Improvement over uniform ---\n      improvement_uncertainty_vs_uniform: 0.085  # 8.5% RMSE improvement\n      improvement_cate_weighted_vs_uniform: 0.134 # 13.4% improvement\n      # --- But gains are modest ---\n      improvement_cate_weighted_vs_uncertainty: 0.053  # only 5.3% beyond uncertainty-only\n      # --- Practical issue: needs pilot CATE estimates ---\n      pilot_fraction_needed: 0.15              # 15% of budget for pilot\n      pilot_quality_sensitivity: \"moderate\"     # noisy pilot → suboptimal allocation\n    result_rationale: >\n      Adaptive allocation 的改进存在但 modest（13.4% over uniform），因为 median 档下\n      subgroup 间的 CATE heterogeneity 较温和——如果 CATE 相差不大，把更多 labels 分给\n      high-CATE subgroups 的 marginal value 有限。CATE-weighted 比 uncertainty-only 仅多 5.3%，\n      因为 high-error subgroups（uncertainty-only targets）和 high-CATE subgroups 有较大 overlap\n      （LLM 在 harder subgroups 上通常 error 更高，而 harder subgroups 往往有 larger effects）。\n      Pilot fraction 15% 进一步 eats into available budget。P2 优先级合理——收入产出比有限。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T14\"\n        caption: \"Allocation strategy comparison (n_expert=250, K=4, extreme regime)\"\n        columns: [\"Strategy\", \"RMSE\", \"Improvement vs Uniform\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Uniform\", \"0.082\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Uncertainty-only\", \"0.075\", \"8.5%\"]\n          - [\"CATE-weighted\", \"0.071\", \"13.4%\"]\n          - [\"Oracle\", \"0.065\", \"20.7%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: RMSE vs allocation strategy bar chart. Diminishing returns visible from uniform → uncertainty → CATE-weighted → oracle.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix 级别结果。CATE-weighted allocation 有理论吸引力但实际改进有限，\n      且需要额外的 pilot phase。推荐在论文中作为 \"extension\" 简要提及，\n      detailed results in appendix。如果 page budget 紧张，可以完全省略。\n\n  - name: \"Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      Test EC-HTE when subgroups are noisy/overlapping or when the true subgroup structure\n      doesn't align with the conditioning variable.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Scenario 1: Noisy subgroup assignment (10% mislabeling) ---\n      echte_rmse_clean_subgroups: 0.072\n      echte_rmse_10pct_noise: 0.085            # 18% RMSE degradation\n      echte_rmse_20pct_noise: 0.105            # 46% degradation\n      echte_rmse_30pct_noise: 0.132            # approaches global correction level\n      # --- Scenario 2: True K=4 but model uses K=2 ---\n      echte_rmse_correct_K4: 0.082\n      echte_rmse_misspecified_K2: 0.098        # 20% degradation\n      echte_rmse_overspecified_K8: 0.095       # 16% degradation from small-sample variance\n      # --- Scenario 3: Continuous moderator discretized ---\n      echte_rmse_correct_discretization: 0.075\n      echte_rmse_coarse_discretization: 0.092  # lose granularity\n      echte_rmse_fine_discretization: 0.098    # too many subgroups, insufficient data\n      # --- HB vs MLE under misspecification ---\n      hb_degradation_10pct_noise: 0.15         # 15% RMSE increase\n      mle_degradation_10pct_noise: 0.25        # 25% RMSE increase — HB more robust\n      hb_degradation_misspecified_K: 0.18\n      mle_degradation_misspecified_K: 0.30\n      # --- \"Graceful degradation\" metric ---\n      echte_worse_than_no_correction_at_noise: 0.35  # EC-HTE becomes worse than no-correction at 35% subgroup noise\n      global_worse_than_no_correction_at_noise: 0.05  # global becomes worse at 5% error heterogeneity — much less robust\n    result_rationale: >\n      Robustness analysis 在 median 档下展示 \"graceful degradation\"——EC-HTE 在 misspecification\n      下性能降低但 gradually，不会 catastrophically fail 直到 noise 极高（35%）。\n      对比 global correction 在 5% heterogeneity 时就变 harmful，EC-HTE 的 robustness 优势明显。\n\n      10% subgroup noise 导致 18% RMSE degradation 的原因：noisy subgroup assignment\n      意味着混淆矩阵估计混合了来自错误 subgroup 的 labels，导致 per-subgroup correction\n      偏向 global（因为混合了多个 subgroup 的 signal）。HB 的 partial pooling 在这里帮助——\n      当 subgroup signal 被 noise 稀释时，HB 自动 shrink toward global，而 MLE 会 fit noise。\n      这是 HB \"never worse than global\" 性质的又一体现。\n\n      Misspecified K（真实 K=4，模型用 K=2）损失 20% 是因为 K=2 将两对不同的 subgroups\n      合并，部分丧失了 stratification 的精确性。但 K=2 仍远优于 global（0.098 vs ~0.19），\n      说明 even coarse stratification helps。Overspecified K=8 的 16% degradation\n      来自 small-sample variance（n/8 per subgroup），与 exp-006 的发现一致。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T15\"\n        caption: \"Robustness: EC-HTE RMSE under subgroup misspecification\"\n        columns: [\"Scenario\", \"Clean\", \"Mild Misspec.\", \"Moderate Misspec.\", \"Severe Misspec.\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Subgroup noise\", \"0.072 (0%)\", \"0.085 (10%)\", \"0.105 (20%)\", \"0.132 (30%)\"]\n          - [\"K misspecification\", \"0.082 (K=4)\", \"0.098 (K=2)\", \"0.095 (K=8)\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Discretization\", \"0.075 (correct)\", \"0.092 (coarse)\", \"0.098 (fine)\", \"—\"]\n      - table_id: \"T16\"\n        caption: \"HB vs MLE degradation under misspecification\"\n        columns: [\"Misspecification\", \"HB RMSE increase\", \"MLE RMSE increase\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"10% subgroup noise\", \"15%\", \"25%\"]\n          - [\"20% subgroup noise\", \"30%\", \"50%\"]\n          - [\"K=4→K=2\", \"18%\", \"30%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: RMSE vs subgroup noise level (0-40%), three lines: EC-HTE, global correction, no correction. Shows EC-HTE crossing no-correction at ~35% noise, global crossing at ~5% heterogeneity. Key message: EC-HTE degrades gracefully.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Robustness 是 median 档下补偿理论锐度不足的关键 empirical contribution。\n      \"EC-HTE is robust to 10-20% subgroup misspecification while global correction breaks at 5%\n      error heterogeneity\" 是有力的 practical message。HB 在 misspecification 下比 MLE 的优势\n      （15% vs 25% degradation）比在 correctly-specified 设定下更明显——\n      这支持 \"HB as robustness guarantee\" 的 narrative pivot。\n      建议将 Fig (RMSE vs noise) 放入 main paper 作为 robustness 的 key visualization。\n\n  - name: \"Causal Forest Integration\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      Apply EC-HTE post-hoc correction to CausalForestDML subgroup CATE estimates +\n      leaf-level corrected pseudo-outcomes with variance-adjusted CIs.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Post-hoc correction of forest subgroup CATEs ---\n      cf_naive_subgroup_bias: 0.12\n      cf_global_corrected_subgroup_bias: 0.17  # global correction still hurts\n      cf_echte_corrected_subgroup_bias: 0.06\n      cf_oracle_corrected_subgroup_bias: 0.03\n      # --- Leaf-level correction ---\n      cf_leaf_naive_rmse: 0.22\n      cf_leaf_echte_rmse: 0.18                 # modest improvement at leaf level\n      cf_leaf_global_rmse: 0.26                # global hurts at leaf level too\n      # --- Variance-adjusted CIs ---\n      cf_echte_coverage_subgroup: 0.90\n      cf_echte_coverage_leaf: 0.87             # harder to cover at leaf level\n      cf_naive_coverage_subgroup: 0.82\n      cf_naive_coverage_leaf: 0.79\n      # --- Comparison with diff-in-means ---\n      dim_echte_rmse: 0.072                    # from exp-001\n      cf_echte_rmse: 0.065                     # CF slightly better due to flexibility\n      cf_advantage_over_dim: 0.10              # 10% RMSE improvement\n    result_rationale: >\n      Causal forest integration 在 median 档下显示 EC-HTE 的 correction 与 CATE estimator\n      choice 正交——bias mechanism 和 correction 适用于任何 estimator。Global correction\n      在 CF 输出上同样 harmful（0.17 vs naive 0.12），EC-HTE 同样 helpful（0.06）。\n\n      Leaf-level correction 比 subgroup-level improvement 更 modest（0.22→0.18 vs 0.12→0.06）\n      因为 leaves 的 granularity 超过 confusion matrix estimation 的 resolution——\n      一个 leaf 可能包含多个 subgroup 的混合，使得 subgroup-specific correction 只是 partial fix。\n      Coverage 在 leaf level 更差（87%）因为 leaf-level CATE variance 本身更大且 harder to estimate。\n\n      CF vs diff-in-means 的 10% advantage 说明 estimator choice matters but is secondary\n      to the correction method choice。论文 message：EC-HTE 是 estimator-agnostic 的 correction\n      layer。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T17\"\n        caption: \"EC-HTE with CausalForestDML: subgroup and leaf-level results\"\n        columns: [\"Level\", \"Naive\", \"Global\", \"EC-HTE\", \"Oracle\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Subgroup CATE bias\", \"0.12\", \"0.17\", \"0.06\", \"0.03\"]\n          - [\"Subgroup coverage\", \"0.82\", \"0.75\", \"0.90\", \"0.94\"]\n          - [\"Leaf CATE RMSE\", \"0.22\", \"0.26\", \"0.18\", \"0.14\"]\n          - [\"Leaf coverage\", \"0.79\", \"0.72\", \"0.87\", \"0.93\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: CATE heterogeneity plot (forest-based) with and without EC-HTE correction. Shows correction preserving heterogeneity structure while reducing bias.\"\n    analysis: >\n      P1 实验，main paper 中简要展示 subgroup-level 结果即可。Leaf-level 分析可放 appendix。\n      核心 takeaway：EC-HTE is estimator-agnostic。CF 的 flexibility 提供 modest additional\n      improvement over diff-in-means，但不是论文的重点。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10224,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10224},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bab92f78-da56-473f-9e96-ce17b8b932a9","uuid":"adceece0-4737-4da4-a37b-3a895e1df16b"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":334903,"duration_api_ms":336187,"num_turns":1,"result":"Looking at the experiment plan and median tier definition, I'll generate the detailed imagined data.\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claims 需降级但不改方向。Claim 1 从 \"5-10x\" 改为 \"up to Nx in high-heterogeneity regimes\"，\n  强调 regime-dependent。Claim 2 中 HB 的 value proposition 从 \"RMSE reduction\" 转向\n  \"automatic robustness guarantee\"（never-worse-than-global），弱化绝对性能优势。Claim 3 诊断准则\n  从 \"sharp threshold\" 改为 \"useful screening tool with practitioner-chosen operating point\"。\n  K>2 需加 Remark 说明高阶项但非完整理论。PPCI 比较需要 Table 精确列出各场景差异，\n  避免简单正交叙事。补充 robustness analysis（exp-010）展示 graceful degradation。\n  论文仍可投 EMNLP main，但需要更多 empirical depth 补偿理论锐度不足。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Hierarchical Bayesian Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator with partial pooling,\n      compared against MLE/Laplace on full regime sweep (extreme/moderate/homogeneous ×\n      n_expert 100-2000 × K=2,4). MCMC via PyMC NUTS, 4 chains, 1500 warmup, 1000 draws.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- HB vs MLE RMSE (subgroup CATE bias) ---\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n100_K2_extreme: 0.72   # HB RMSE / MLE RMSE ratio — HB wins big at small n\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n250_K2_extreme: 0.88   # advantage narrows\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n500_K2_extreme: 0.95   # marginal at n=500\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n1000_K2_extreme: 0.98  # essentially tied\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n250_K2_moderate: 0.93  # moderate regime — less room to improve\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n250_K2_homogeneous: 0.99  # homogeneous — no benefit, no harm\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n100_K4_extreme: 0.65   # K=4 + small n — HB shines\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n250_K4_extreme: 0.82   # K=4 still benefits more than K=2\n      hb_rmse_vs_mle_n500_K4_extreme: 0.91\n      # --- Coverage (nominal 95%) ---\n      coverage_hb_n250_K2_extreme: 0.91       # slight undercoverage\n      coverage_hb_n500_K2_extreme: 0.93\n      coverage_hb_n1000_K2_extreme: 0.94\n      coverage_hb_n250_K4_extreme: 0.89       # K=4 worse — more parameters, less data per cell\n      coverage_hb_n500_K4_extreme: 0.91\n      coverage_mle_n250_K2_extreme: 0.83      # MLE substantially undercovered\n      coverage_mle_n500_K2_extreme: 0.89\n      coverage_laplace_n250_K2_extreme: 0.87  # Laplace between MLE and HB\n      # --- MCMC diagnostics ---\n      rhat_max_across_params: 1.003\n      ess_bulk_min: 380\n      ess_tail_min: 220\n      divergences_per_chain: 0\n      mcmc_runtime_seconds_per_mc_rep: 4.2    # ~4s per MCMC fit\n      mle_runtime_seconds_per_mc_rep: 0.02\n      runtime_ratio_hb_vs_mle: 210\n      # --- Never-worse-than-global guarantee ---\n      hb_worse_than_global_fraction: 0.0      # HB never worse than global across all settings\n      hb_worse_than_mle_fraction_n1000: 0.03  # at large n, HB occasionally trivially worse than MLE\n      # --- Total MC runs ---\n      total_mc_reps: 1000\n      se_on_rmse_ratio: 0.008                 # SE of RMSE ratio estimate\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 HB partial pooling 的 value proposition 在 n_expert<150 时显著，n=250 时边际。\n      原因：Dirichlet 先验在小样本时提供正则化，将不稳定的 per-subgroup MLE 估计向全局均值收缩，\n      避免极端的混淆矩阵估计导致的 CATE 校正爆炸。但当 n_expert 足够大（≥500），MLE 本身已稳定，\n      HB 的收缩几乎不改变估计。K=4 下 HB 优势更持久是因为每个 subgroup 分到的样本更少（n/K），\n      收缩效应持续到更大的 n。Coverage 存在轻微 undercoverage（89-93%）而非理论 95%，\n      原因是 posterior variance 未完全捕捉混淆矩阵估计误差向 CATE 校正的非线性传播——\n      delta method 近似 underestimates variance。MCMC 诊断干净（R̂<1.01, ESS>200），\n      但运行时间比 MLE 慢 200x，需在论文中讨论实际部署 trade-off。\n      关键发现：HB 的 \"never worse than global\" 性质在所有 setting 下成立——这是因为\n      partial pooling 在 data-poor 时自动退化为 global estimator，在 data-rich 时退化为 stratified MLE，\n      提供单调改进保证。这成为 median 档下 HB 的核心卖点，替代绝对 RMSE 优势。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T1\"\n        caption: \"HB vs MLE vs Laplace: RMSE ratio and coverage across regimes (K=2)\"\n        columns: [\"regime\", \"n_expert\", \"HB/MLE RMSE\", \"HB Coverage\", \"MLE Coverage\", \"Laplace Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"extreme\", 100, \"0.72 (0.02)\", \"0.90 (0.01)\", \"0.79 (0.02)\", \"0.84 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 250, \"0.88 (0.01)\", \"0.91 (0.01)\", \"0.83 (0.01)\", \"0.87 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 500, \"0.95 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\", \"0.89 (0.01)\", \"0.91 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 1000, \"0.98 (0.01)\", \"0.94 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"moderate\", 250, \"0.93 (0.01)\", \"0.92 (0.01)\", \"0.87 (0.01)\", \"0.89 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"homogeneous\", 250, \"0.99 (0.01)\", \"0.94 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\"]\n      - table_id: \"T2\"\n        caption: \"HB vs MLE: RMSE ratio across regimes (K=4)\"\n        columns: [\"regime\", \"n_expert\", \"HB/MLE RMSE\", \"HB Coverage\", \"MLE Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"extreme\", 100, \"0.65 (0.02)\", \"0.88 (0.01)\", \"0.72 (0.02)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 250, \"0.82 (0.01)\", \"0.89 (0.01)\", \"0.80 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 500, \"0.91 (0.01)\", \"0.91 (0.01)\", \"0.86 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"extreme\", 1000, \"0.97 (0.01)\", \"0.93 (0.01)\", \"0.91 (0.01)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: RMSE ratio (HB/MLE) vs n_expert curves, separate lines for K=2 and K=4, shaded 95% CI bands. Shows HB advantage decaying toward 1.0 as n grows, with K=4 curve consistently below K=2.\"\n      - \"Fig: Coverage vs n_expert, three estimators (HB/MLE/Laplace), horizontal dashed line at 0.95. Shows all undercovering but HB closest to nominal.\"\n    analysis: >\n      HB 的核心价值不在绝对 RMSE 优势（n=250 时仅 12% improvement for K=2），而在两个性质：\n      (1) never-worse-than-global 保证——在 homogeneous regime 下自动收缩回 global，无需 practitioner\n      判断何时该 stratify；(2) K=4 下优势显著持久——实际应用中 subgroup 数常 >2。\n      Undercoverage 问题（88-93% vs nominal 95%）需在论文中诊断：主要原因是 confusion matrix\n      uncertainty 通过矩阵求逆向 CATE 传播时的非线性效应被 delta-method 低估。建议加 Remark\n      说明并推荐 posterior predictive check 作为实践中的 calibration 工具。\n      Runtime 210x overhead 在 MC simulation 中累积严重（4.2s × 1000 reps = 70 min per setting），\n      但实际应用只需 fit 一次，4s 完全可接受。\n\n  - name: \"Bias Bound Verification (K=2 and K=4)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      Derive analytic bias formula bias ∝ Δπ×Δτ for K=2, verify empirically on systematic\n      parameter grid, extend to K=4 with sum-of-products form, assess R² of analytic\n      prediction vs MC simulation.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- K=2 bias formula verification ---\n      r_squared_K2_analytic_vs_mc: 0.89       # good but not perfect fit\n      r_squared_K2_with_intercept: 0.91       # allowing intercept slightly improves\n      bias_bound_tightness_ratio_K2_median: 1.15  # analytic bound / MC bias — slightly loose\n      bias_bound_tightness_ratio_K2_p90: 1.45     # tail cases where bound is loose\n      # --- K=4 extension ---\n      r_squared_K4_sum_of_products: 0.76      # K=4 substantially worse with simple formula\n      r_squared_K4_with_interaction_terms: 0.84  # adding pairwise interactions helps\n      r_squared_K4_full_model: 0.88           # with all higher-order terms, recovers K=2 quality\n      # --- \"Debiasing can hurt\" proposition ---\n      bias_amplification_extreme_regime: 4.2   # global correction / no correction bias ratio\n      bias_amplification_moderate_regime: 2.3\n      bias_amplification_homogeneous_regime: 1.05  # near 1 — global doesn't hurt when homogeneous\n      # --- Parameter grid coverage ---\n      n_grid_points_delta_pi: 10              # Δπ from 0.02 to 0.25\n      n_grid_points_delta_tau: 10             # Δτ from 0.05 to 0.50\n      n_mc_reps_per_point: 1000\n      se_on_bias_ratio: 0.05\n      # --- Specific constructive example (two-subgroup) ---\n      constructive_example_subgroup1_bias_global: 0.18    # over-correction\n      constructive_example_subgroup2_bias_global: -0.14   # under-correction\n      constructive_example_aggregate_looks_ok: true        # aggregate bias ~0.02, masks subgroup issue\n      constructive_example_subgroup1_bias_nocorrection: 0.04\n      constructive_example_subgroup2_bias_nocorrection: -0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 K=2 的 R²≥0.85 但非 0.95+，因为 Δπ×Δτ 是一阶近似——忽略了混淆矩阵\n      off-diagonal 的二阶交互以及样本量有限时的随机波动。在 Δπ 或 Δτ 极端时（>0.15 或 >0.35），\n      non-linear terms 变得 non-negligible，拖低整体 R²。R²=0.89 意味着 Δπ×Δτ 捕捉了 89%\n      的 systematic variation——足够作为诊断工具的理论基础，但需要在论文中明确标注 \"first-order\n      approximation\" 而非 \"exact characterization\"。\n\n      K=4 下 R² 显著下降至 0.76 是因为 K=4 有 C(4,2)=6 个 subgroup pair 的交互，\n      简单 sum-of-products Σ(Δπ_k × Δτ_k) 忽略了 cross-subgroup misclassification routing\n      （subgroup A 的样本被误分到 subgroup B 而非 C 的具体 pattern 不被 marginal Δπ 捕捉）。\n      加入 pairwise interaction terms 后恢复到 0.84，说明 K>2 的理论需要更精细的建模。\n      这支持论文中加 Remark 而非完整 K>2 定理。\n\n      Bias amplification 在 extreme regime 达到 4.2x（而非 framing 中的 5-10x）——\n      这是因为 \"5-10x\" 需要非常极端的参数组合（Δπ>0.15 且 Δτ>0.3），median 档下\n      semi-synthetic 数据中的 LLM 误分类异质性较温和，实际 Δπ 多在 0.05-0.12 范围。\n      论文需将 headline 从 \"5-10x\" 改为 \"up to 4-5x in high-heterogeneity regimes\"。\n\n      Constructive two-subgroup example 的关键 insight：aggregate bias 接近 0（0.02），\n      因为 over-correction 和 under-correction 部分抵消。这意味着仅看 aggregate metrics\n      的研究者会认为 global correction 工作良好，而实际 subgroup-level bias 高达 0.18。\n      这是 paper 的核心 narrative hook。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T3\"\n        caption: \"Analytic bias bound R² by K and model specification\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"Model\", \"R²\", \"Bound tightness (median)\", \"Bound tightness (90th pct)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [2, \"Δπ×Δτ (no intercept)\", \"0.89\", \"1.15\", \"1.45\"]\n          - [2, \"Δπ×Δτ (with intercept)\", \"0.91\", \"1.12\", \"1.38\"]\n          - [4, \"Σ(Δπ_k×Δτ_k)\", \"0.76\", \"1.32\", \"1.85\"]\n          - [4, \"+ pairwise interactions\", \"0.84\", \"1.20\", \"1.55\"]\n          - [4, \"+ all higher-order\", \"0.88\", \"1.14\", \"1.42\"]\n      - table_id: \"T4\"\n        caption: \"Bias amplification factor (global correction / no correction) by regime\"\n        columns: [\"regime\", \"Δπ range\", \"Δτ range\", \"amplification (mean ± SE)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"extreme\", \"0.10-0.25\", \"0.20-0.50\", \"4.2 ± 0.3\"]\n          - [\"moderate\", \"0.05-0.12\", \"0.10-0.25\", \"2.3 ± 0.2\"]\n          - [\"mild\", \"0.02-0.05\", \"0.05-0.12\", \"1.4 ± 0.1\"]\n          - [\"homogeneous\", \"< 0.02\", \"any\", \"1.05 ± 0.05\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Bias amplification heatmap — x-axis Δπ (0.02-0.25), y-axis Δτ (0.05-0.50), color = global/no-correction bias ratio. Diagonal contour lines show iso-amplification. Clear gradient from bottom-left (≈1) to top-right (≈5). Key for paper Figure 2.\"\n      - \"Fig: Analytic prediction vs MC bias scatter plot, K=2 and K=4 side by side. K=2 tightly clustered around 45° line; K=4 shows more dispersion, especially at high bias values.\"\n      - \"Fig: Constructive two-subgroup example bar chart — subgroup 1 and 2 bias under no-correction, global correction, and EC-HTE. Shows global correction flipping sign of bias for subgroup 1.\"\n    analysis: >\n      R²=0.89 (K=2) 足够支撑 diagnostic criterion 但需要 honest framing：论文应写\n      \"the Δπ×Δτ product explains ~90% of bias variance in the K=2 setting\"\n      而非 \"bias is exactly proportional to Δπ×Δτ\"。K=4 的 R²=0.76 是写 Remark 而非 Theorem\n      的理由——可以说 \"empirically the sum-of-products form captures the dominant variation\n      but cross-subgroup misclassification routing introduces additional structure not\n      captured by marginal heterogeneity measures\"。这反而可以作为 future work 的自然 hook。\n      Bias amplification 4.2x（非 7.8x）意味着 headline 需要调整。可以在 abstract 中写\n      \"up to 4x in realistic settings\"，在 appendix 中展示极端参数下理论上可达更高倍数。\n\n  - name: \"Semi-Synthetic Political Science Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      Real political-science tweet corpus with injected CATE heterogeneity structure,\n      annotated by GPT-4.1 and Qwen3-235B-A22B. Measure subgroup-specific misclassification\n      rates, apply EC-HTE vs baselines (no correction, global correction, MLE stratified,\n      HB stratified).\n    expected_results:\n      # --- LLM annotation quality ---\n      gpt4_overall_accuracy: 0.82\n      gpt4_subgroup_accuracy_range: [0.75, 0.88]   # max/min ratio ~1.17\n      gpt4_misclass_heterogeneity_delta_pi_max: 0.09\n      qwen3_overall_accuracy: 0.76\n      qwen3_subgroup_accuracy_range: [0.67, 0.83]   # max/min ratio ~1.24\n      qwen3_misclass_heterogeneity_delta_pi_max: 0.13\n      # --- CATE bias results (primary) ---\n      # subgroup CATE RMSE across methods — n_expert=500, K=2\n      rmse_no_correction: 0.145\n      rmse_global_correction: 0.198           # global makes it worse\n      rmse_mle_stratified: 0.078\n      rmse_hb_stratified: 0.072               # HB marginally better than MLE at n=500\n      rmse_oracle_stratified: 0.035           # oracle = true confusion matrices\n      # --- Bias amplification ---\n      bias_amplification_gpt4: 2.8            # global/no-correction on GPT-4.1 annotations\n      bias_amplification_qwen3: 3.6           # worse for noisier annotator\n      # --- EC-HTE subgroup bias reduction vs global ---\n      ec_hte_bias_reduction_vs_global_gpt4: 0.72   # EC-HTE subgroup bias / global subgroup bias\n      ec_hte_bias_reduction_vs_global_qwen3: 0.65\n      # --- Coverage ---\n      coverage_hb_gpt4_n500: 0.91\n      coverage_hb_qwen3_n500: 0.89\n      coverage_global_gpt4_n500: 0.78\n      # --- Sample sizes ---\n      n_tweets_total: 12000\n      n_expert_labels: 500\n      n_subgroups: 2\n      # --- Causal estimator ---\n      cate_estimator: \"difference-in-means within strata\"\n      injected_cate_subgroup1: 0.15\n      injected_cate_subgroup2: 0.35\n      injected_delta_tau: 0.20\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 LLM 误分类异质性存在但较温和（max/min accuracy ratio 1.17-1.24），\n      这是因为现代 LLMs（GPT-4.1, Qwen3）的分类能力已较强，subgroup 间的 accuracy 差异\n      主要来自 label ambiguity 和 subgroup-specific language patterns，而非系统性能力差异。\n      GPT-4.1 的 Δπ_max=0.09 对应于 bias amplification 2.8x——低于 framing 中的 5-10x\n      但仍然实质性。Qwen3 因整体质量更低，Δπ_max=0.13，amplification 达到 3.6x。\n\n      HB vs MLE 在 n_expert=500 时仅有 marginal improvement（0.072 vs 0.078 RMSE）——\n      这与 exp-001 的发现一致：n=500/K=2=250 per subgroup，已足够 MLE 稳定。\n      论文需要在此处强调 HB 的 robustness guarantee 而非 RMSE improvement。\n\n      EC-HTE bias reduction vs global 在 0.65-0.72 范围——显著但非 dramatic。这意味着\n      EC-HTE 将 global correction 的 subgroup bias 减少了 28-35%，而非消除。残余 bias\n      来自有限 expert labels 下混淆矩阵估计的噪声（非系统性的）。\n\n      Coverage 89-91% 而非 95% 延续了 exp-001 的 undercoverage pattern。在 semi-synthetic\n      setting 中这更显著因为 injected CATE structure 的复杂性超过了纯 synthetic 的简单设定。\n\n      Qwen3 的 bias amplification (3.6x) > GPT-4.1 (2.8x) 提供了一个自然的 narrative：\n      \"lower-quality annotators produce more heterogeneous errors, making the bias mechanism\n      more severe — precisely the setting where EC-HTE is most needed\"。这是论文的关键 empirical\n      point。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T5\"\n        caption: \"Semi-synthetic benchmark: subgroup CATE estimation across methods (K=2, n_expert=500)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Subgroup 1 Bias\", \"Subgroup 2 Bias\", \"RMSE\", \"Coverage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"No correction\", \"0.08 (0.02)\", \"-0.11 (0.02)\", \"0.145 (0.008)\", \"0.85 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"Global correction\", \"-0.14 (0.03)\", \"0.15 (0.03)\", \"0.198 (0.012)\", \"0.78 (0.02)\"]\n          - [\"MLE stratified\", \"0.02 (0.03)\", \"-0.03 (0.03)\", \"0.078 (0.010)\", \"0.87 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"HB stratified (EC-HTE)\", \"0.01 (0.02)\", \"-0.02 (0.02)\", \"0.072 (0.008)\", \"0.91 (0.01)\"]\n          - [\"Oracle stratified\", \"0.00 (0.01)\", \"0.00 (0.01)\", \"0.035 (0.004)\", \"0.95 (0.01)\"]\n      - table_id: \"T6\"\n        caption: \"LLM annotation quality by subgroup\"\n        columns: [\"LLM\", \"Overall Acc\", \"Subgroup 1 Acc\", \"Subgroup 2 Acc\", \"Δπ_max\", \"Bias Amplification\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4.1\", \"0.82\", \"0.88\", \"0.75\", \"0.09\", \"2.8\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-235B\", \"0.76\", \"0.83\", \"0.67\", \"0.13\", \"3.6\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Subgroup bias bar chart — 4 methods × 2 subgroups, showing sign flip under global correction. Key paper Figure 3.\"\n      - \"Fig: Bias amplification scatter — x-axis Δπ (from both LLMs), y-axis amplification factor, with analytic prediction line from exp-002 overlaid. Shows semi-synthetic points fall near analytic prediction.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Semi-synthetic 结果与 synthetic (exp-001/002) 的一致性是关键：analytic prediction (exp-002)\n      预测 Δπ=0.09 时 amplification ~2.5-3x，实际 GPT-4.1 得到 2.8x，验证了理论。\n      但 LLM 误分类异质性较温和（ratio 1.17-1.24 vs 需要 >1.5 才能产生 dramatic effects），\n      这是 median 档的核心特征——效应存在但需要选择性展示 regime。论文策略：用 Qwen3（更大异质性）\n      作为 primary showcase，GPT-4.1 作为 \"even with a good annotator, the effect exists\" 的补充。\n      Oracle RMSE (0.035) vs EC-HTE (0.072) 的 gap 说明混淆矩阵估计的 noise floor 是实际瓶颈，\n      不是方法本身的系统偏差——这支持 \"more expert labels always help\" 的 message。\n\n  - name: \"Real-Data Validation (Ashwin et al.)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Apply EC-HTE to Ashwin et al. (2025) Rohingya refugee interview dataset where\n      LLM annotation errors correlate with refugee status, gender, education.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Dataset characteristics ---\n      n_interviews: 1800\n      n_expert_coded: 400                      # subset with expert labels\n      annotation_categories: 5                 # trauma, resilience, agency, blame, neutral\n      subgroups_by: \"refugee_status × gender\"  # 2×2 = 4 cells\n      # --- LLM annotation heterogeneity ---\n      gpt4_overall_accuracy_5class: 0.68\n      gpt4_accuracy_range_by_subgroup: [0.58, 0.76]  # substantial heterogeneity\n      gpt4_delta_pi_max: 0.14\n      # --- CATE results (treatment = interview framing) ---\n      cate_global_correction_bias_worst_subgroup: 0.22\n      cate_no_correction_bias_worst_subgroup: 0.09\n      cate_echte_bias_worst_subgroup: 0.05\n      bias_amplification_global: 3.1\n      # --- But real data is messy ---\n      cate_uncertainty_wide: true               # CIs are wide due to small n per cell\n      echte_vs_mle_difference_significant: false # p=0.18 for RMSE difference\n      coverage_hb: 0.90\n      coverage_global: 0.74\n      # --- Qualitative findings ---\n      worst_subgroup: \"female refugees\"         # highest misclassification, highest CATE\n      best_subgroup: \"male host community\"      # lowest misclassification\n      bias_direction_global: \"over-correction of male host community, under-correction of female refugees\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Real data 验证在 median 档下呈现 \"directionally correct but noisy\" 的模式。\n      Ashwin et al. 数据的 5-class 分类比 binary 更难，GPT-4.1 overall accuracy 仅 0.68，\n      且 refugee status × gender 产生的 subgroup 异质性（0.58-0.76）比 semi-synthetic 更大——\n      这是因为 LLM 在处理 trauma-related narratives 时，对女性难民的文化特定表达识别率更低。\n\n      Bias amplification 3.1x 与 semi-synthetic 一致，但因为 real data 的 treatment effect\n      本身 uncertainty 更大（不是 injected 的），EC-HTE vs MLE 的差异在统计上不显著（p=0.18）。\n      这是 median 档的典型 real-data 结果：方向正确但 power 不足以宣称显著优势。\n\n      论文策略：将 real-data 作为 \"proof of concept\" 而非 \"primary evidence\"，\n      强调 bias mechanism 在 real data 中确实存在（global correction 的 worst-subgroup bias\n      0.22 vs no-correction 的 0.09），EC-HTE 改善方向正确（0.05），但承认 sample size\n      限制了 statistical power。Coverage 差异（0.90 vs 0.74）在 real data 中尤其有意义——\n      global correction 的 CI 严重 miscalibrated。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T7\"\n        caption: \"Ashwin et al. real-data: worst-subgroup CATE bias by method\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Worst subgroup bias\", \"Mean abs bias\", \"Coverage\", \"CI width\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"No correction\", \"0.09\", \"0.06\", \"0.86\", \"0.28\"]\n          - [\"Global correction\", \"0.22\", \"0.14\", \"0.74\", \"0.25\"]\n          - [\"MLE stratified\", \"0.07\", \"0.05\", \"0.83\", \"0.35\"]\n          - [\"HB stratified (EC-HTE)\", \"0.05\", \"0.03\", \"0.90\", \"0.32\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Heatmap of LLM accuracy by subgroup (refugee_status × gender × annotation_category). Shows clear pattern of lower accuracy for female refugees on trauma/agency categories.\"\n      - \"Fig: CATE estimates ± CI by subgroup, 4 methods side by side. Shows global correction distorting relative ordering of subgroup effects.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Real data 中最有价值的发现是 bias 的 substantive interpretation：global correction\n      系统性低估 female refugees 的 treatment effect 同时高估 male host community——\n      这有直接的 policy relevance（错误的 subgroup 优先级排序）。即使 EC-HTE 的 statistical\n      improvement 边际，correcting the direction of subgroup ranking 具有实际意义。\n      论文应强调这个 qualitative finding 而非纠结 p-value。数据集 4 个 subgroup × 400 expert\n      labels 意味着每个 cell ~100 个 labels，处于 HB 优势最明显的 regime（与 exp-001 一致）。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Criterion Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Compute misclass_heterogeneity × CATE_heterogeneity product from pilot data,\n      evaluate as binary classifier for \"global correction is harmful\". ROC analysis.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Diagnostic performance ---\n      diagnostic_auc: 0.82                     # moderate, not sharp\n      diagnostic_auc_ci_95: [0.77, 0.87]\n      # --- Operating point analysis ---\n      threshold_high_sensitivity: 0.015        # catches 90% of harmful cases\n      sensitivity_at_high_threshold: 0.90\n      specificity_at_high_threshold: 0.55      # many false alarms\n      threshold_balanced: 0.035                # balanced operating point\n      sensitivity_at_balanced: 0.75\n      specificity_at_balanced: 0.72\n      threshold_high_specificity: 0.065        # few false alarms\n      sensitivity_at_high_specificity: 0.55\n      specificity_at_high_specificity: 0.90\n      # --- Where the gray zone is ---\n      gray_zone_product_range: [0.02, 0.06]    # ambiguous zone\n      fraction_settings_in_gray_zone: 0.35     # 35% of settings fall here\n      # --- Comparison to simpler diagnostics ---\n      auc_delta_pi_only: 0.73                  # misclass heterogeneity alone\n      auc_delta_tau_only: 0.65                 # CATE heterogeneity alone\n      auc_product_advantage_over_best_single: 0.09  # product adds 9 AUC points\n      # --- From different data sources ---\n      auc_using_synthetic_threshold_on_semisynthetic: 0.79  # slight degradation on transfer\n      auc_on_real_data_ashwin: 0.78            # further degradation on real\n    result_rationale: >\n      AUC=0.82 而非 >0.90 的原因：diagnostic product Δπ×Δτ 是 bias 的一阶近似（exp-002\n      已展示 R²=0.89），但将 continuous bias magnitude 转为 binary \"harmful/not harmful\"\n      引入了 threshold-dependent noise——接近 boundary 的 cases 本质上模糊。此外，\n      \"harmful\" 的定义本身有 arbitrariness（global bias > 1.5x no-correction? 2x? depends on\n      acceptable bias level），不同的 ground truth definition 改变 AUC ±0.03。\n\n      35% 的 settings 落在 gray zone 是 median 档的核心特征——实际数据中 Δπ 和 Δτ\n      往往不极端，导致大量 \"depends on your tolerance\" cases。这迫使论文从 \"sharp threshold\"\n      转向 \"practitioner-chosen operating point\" 的 framing。\n\n      Product 比单一 metric 强 9 AUC points（0.82 vs 0.73），证明了两个维度的交互信息——\n      但不是 dramatic improvement。Δπ alone AUC=0.73 说明即使只看误分类异质性也有一定诊断力。\n\n      Transfer performance 从 synthetic (AUC=0.82) 到 semi-synthetic (0.79) 到 real (0.78)\n      呈现 graceful degradation——阈值具有一定 portability 但非 universal。\n      论文建议 practitioners 用小规模 pilot study 校准阈值。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T8\"\n        caption: \"Diagnostic criterion ROC operating points\"\n        columns: [\"Operating Point\", \"Δπ×Δτ threshold\", \"Sensitivity\", \"Specificity\", \"F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"High sensitivity\", \"0.015\", \"0.90\", \"0.55\", \"0.68\"]\n          - [\"Balanced\", \"0.035\", \"0.75\", \"0.72\", \"0.73\"]\n          - [\"High specificity\", \"0.065\", \"0.55\", \"0.90\", \"0.67\"]\n      - table_id: \"T9\"\n        caption: \"Diagnostic AUC comparison across metrics and data sources\"\n        columns: [\"Diagnostic\", \"Synthetic AUC\", \"Semi-synthetic AUC\", \"Real data AUC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Δπ×Δτ product\", \"0.82\", \"0.79\", \"0.78\"]\n          - [\"Δπ only\", \"0.73\", \"0.71\", \"0.70\"]\n          - [\"Δτ only\", \"0.65\", \"0.64\", \"0.62\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: ROC curve with three operating points marked. Gray shaded area shows the region of Δπ×Δτ ∈ [0.02, 0.06] where the diagnostic is ambiguous. Key paper Figure 4.\"\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot of Δπ×Δτ product vs actual bias amplification factor, colored by data source (synthetic/semi-synthetic/real). Shows positive correlation but substantial scatter in the gray zone.\"\n    analysis: >\n      AUC=0.82 的 diagnostic 定位为 \"useful screening tool\" 而非 \"sharp threshold\"。\n      论文 framing：先计算 Δπ×Δτ 作为 pre-analysis step；若 product < 0.015，global correction\n      likely safe（false negative rate ~10%）；若 > 0.065，strongly recommend stratified\n      correction；中间地带需 domain knowledge。这比 \"compute this number, if >X use EC-HTE\"\n      的 sharp rule 更 honest，也更 useful（给 practitioner 决策权而非 black box）。\n      35% gray zone fraction 是主要 limitation，需在论文中 explicitly discuss。\n\n  - name: \"Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Systematic sweep n_expert ∈ {50, 100, 250, 500, 1000, 2000} × K ∈ {2, 4, 8}.\n      Find crossover where EC-HTE outperforms global. Validate HB value at small n.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Crossover points (EC-HTE RMSE < Global RMSE) ---\n      crossover_n_K2_extreme: 180              # need ~180 expert labels for K=2 extreme\n      crossover_n_K2_moderate: 350             # moderate regime needs more\n      crossover_n_K4_extreme: 320              # K=4 needs more total (but less per subgroup)\n      crossover_n_K4_moderate: 480\n      crossover_n_K8_extreme: 600              # K=8 pushes crossover high\n      crossover_n_K8_moderate: \">1000\"         # may not cross within budget\n      # --- HB vs MLE at crossover ---\n      hb_advantage_at_crossover_K2: 0.15       # 15% RMSE improvement over MLE at crossover\n      hb_advantage_at_crossover_K4: 0.22       # HB more valuable at crossover for K=4\n      hb_advantage_at_crossover_K8: 0.28       # and even more for K=8\n      # --- Budget efficiency ---\n      rmse_hb_n50_K2: 0.185                    # very noisy but still directionally helpful\n      rmse_global_n50_K2: 0.210                # global already harmful\n      rmse_hb_n2000_K2: 0.042                  # close to oracle\n      rmse_oracle_K2: 0.035\n      # --- HB \"never worse than global\" ---\n      hb_worse_than_global_any_setting: false   # confirmed across all n×K\n      mle_worse_than_global_at_n50_K4: true     # MLE can be worse at very small n, large K\n      mle_worse_than_global_at_n50_K8: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Crossover point 在 250-500 范围（取决于 K 和 regime severity）而非更低，\n      因为 stratified correction 需要每个 subgroup 有足够 expert labels 来估计 confusion matrix——\n      at minimum ~30-50 per subgroup for stable estimates。K=2 时 n=180 意味着 ~90 per subgroup，\n      刚好够。K=8 时 n=600 意味着 ~75 per subgroup，也是 marginal。\n\n      HB 的优势在 crossover 附近最大（15-28%），因为这正是 MLE 估计开始不稳定的区域——\n      少几个 labels MLE 完全不可用，多几个 MLE 已经稳定，HB 的 partial pooling 正好填补\n      这个 transition zone。K 越大 transition zone 越宽（每个 subgroup 样本更少），\n      所以 HB 优势越持久。\n\n      K=8 + moderate regime 下 crossover 可能超过 n=1000——这是实际限制，论文需 honestly\n      discuss：EC-HTE 在 K>4 时可能需要不切实际的 expert budget，除非 regime 足够 extreme。\n      这支持 \"use diagnostic criterion first, then decide K granularity\" 的 practical workflow。\n\n      MLE 在 n=50, K≥4 时反而比 global 更差——混淆矩阵估计太噪导致 correction 发散。\n      HB 通过收缩避免了这个问题，证明了 \"never worse than global\" 的 practical value。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T10\"\n        caption: \"Crossover expert budget by K and regime\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"Regime\", \"Crossover n\", \"HB RMSE advantage at crossover\"]\n        rows:\n          - [2, \"extreme\", 180, \"15%\"]\n          - [2, \"moderate\", 350, \"10%\"]\n          - [4, \"extreme\", 320, \"22%\"]\n          - [4, \"moderate\", 480, \"16%\"]\n          - [8, \"extreme\", 600, \"28%\"]\n          - [8, \"moderate\", \">1000\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: RMSE vs n_expert curves, separate panels for K=2,4,8. Three lines per panel: global (flat, high), MLE stratified (decreasing, noisy at small n), HB stratified (decreasing, smooth). Vertical dashed line at crossover point. Key paper Figure 5.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Budget sensitivity 是论文实际建议的基础。Key message：对于典型 NLP-CSS study（K=2-4 subgroups，\n      moderate heterogeneity），250-500 expert labels 是 EC-HTE 的 minimum viable budget。\n      这与 expert annotation 的现实成本兼容（500 labels × $2/label = $1000，typical research budget）。\n      K=8 的高 crossover 是 honest limitation——如果 subgroup structure 太细，需要 unrealistic budget\n      或者 collapse subgroups（HB 自动做的 partial pooling 本质上是 soft collapsing）。\n\n  - name: \"PPCI Baseline Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      Head-to-head comparison with PPCI (Sui et al., 2026) on covariate-side vs outcome-side\n      error. Theoretical discussion of composition. If feasible, combined correction experiment.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Scenario A: Covariate-side error only (EC-HTE's home turf) ---\n      echte_bias_cov_error_only: 0.04\n      ppci_bias_cov_error_only: 0.16           # PPCI doesn't address covariate error\n      global_bias_cov_error_only: 0.19\n      # --- Scenario B: Outcome-side error only (PPCI's home turf) ---\n      echte_bias_outcome_error_only: 0.14      # EC-HTE doesn't address outcome error\n      ppci_bias_outcome_error_only: 0.05\n      global_bias_outcome_error_only: 0.15\n      # --- Scenario C: Both errors present ---\n      echte_bias_both_errors: 0.13\n      ppci_bias_both_errors: 0.15\n      global_bias_both_errors: 0.24\n      combined_echte_ppci_bias: 0.08            # sequential application helps\n      # --- But PPCI partially helps on covariate error in some settings ---\n      ppci_bias_cov_error_high_correlation: 0.11  # when covariate error correlates with outcome\n      ppci_partial_effectiveness_on_cov_error: true\n      # --- Coverage ---\n      coverage_echte_cov_only: 0.91\n      coverage_ppci_cov_only: 0.80\n      coverage_ppci_outcome_only: 0.93\n      coverage_echte_outcome_only: 0.82\n      coverage_combined_both: 0.88\n      # --- PPCI implementation details ---\n      ppci_kernel_bandwidth: \"Silverman rule\"\n      ppci_convergence_rate: \"n^{-2/5} for d=1\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 PPCI 比较的关键 nuance：PPCI 在纯 covariate error setting 下并非完全无效\n      （bias 0.16 vs global 0.19），因为当 covariate error 与 outcome 有相关性时，\n      PPCI 的 kernel localization 间接捕捉了一部分 covariate-side heterogeneity。\n      这破坏了 \"完全正交\" 的简单叙事，需要 table 精确列出每个场景。\n\n      具体原因：PPCI 通过 kernel smoothing 估计 conditional expectation E[Y|X]，\n      当 X 的 misclassification 与 Y 的 noise 结构相关时，PPCI 的 correction 会 \"accidentally\"\n      部分校正 covariate error 的影响。这在 high correlation setting 下更明显（bias 0.11 vs 0.16）。\n      但 EC-HTE 仍然显著更优（0.04 vs 0.11），因为它直接 targets covariate error。\n\n      Combined application（先 EC-HTE 校正 covariate error，再 PPCI 校正 outcome error）\n      在 both-errors 场景下达到 bias 0.08——优于任一单独方法（0.13 和 0.15）。\n      但 coverage 降到 0.88，因为两步校正的 uncertainty 叠加。\n      论文可以讨论 composition 作为 future direction，但 median 档下证据不足以作为主要 claim。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T11\"\n        caption: \"EC-HTE vs PPCI: head-to-head by error type (K=2, n_expert=500)\"\n        columns: [\"Error Type\", \"No Correction\", \"Global\", \"EC-HTE\", \"PPCI\", \"EC-HTE+PPCI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Covariate only\", \"0.12\", \"0.19\", \"0.04\", \"0.16\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Covariate (high corr w/ outcome)\", \"0.12\", \"0.19\", \"0.04\", \"0.11\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Outcome only\", \"0.13\", \"0.15\", \"0.14\", \"0.05\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Both\", \"0.18\", \"0.24\", \"0.13\", \"0.15\", \"0.08\"]\n      - table_id: \"T12\"\n        caption: \"Coverage comparison by error type and method\"\n        columns: [\"Error Type\", \"EC-HTE\", \"PPCI\", \"EC-HTE+PPCI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Covariate only\", \"0.91\", \"0.80\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Outcome only\", \"0.82\", \"0.93\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Both\", \"0.85\", \"0.83\", \"0.88\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 2×2 panel showing bias by method across 4 error scenarios. Highlights that each method excels on its target error type, with partial overlap in high-correlation settings.\"\n    analysis: >\n      PPCI 比较的 takeaway 需要 nuance：不是 \"orthogonal problems, use EC-HTE for covariate error\n      and PPCI for outcome error\"，而是 \"EC-HTE strongly dominates on covariate error;\n      PPCI partially helps on covariate error in correlated settings but EC-HTE is 3-4x better;\n      PPCI strongly dominates on outcome error; composition is promising but needs more work\"。\n      论文 Table 11 是关键——需要 reviewers 看到所有场景而非 cherry-picked 对比。\n      特别要 preempt reviewer 质疑 \"PPCI already partially handles this\"：\n      用 high-correlation scenario 的 0.11 vs 0.04 说明 \"partial ≠ adequate\"。\n\n  - name: \"Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4.1 vs Qwen3-235B-A22B vs Claude Sonnet 4.6: measure misclassification heterogeneity\n      patterns, show EC-HTE benefit varies by LLM quality.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Per-LLM quality ---\n      gpt4_accuracy: 0.82\n      gpt4_delta_pi_max: 0.09\n      gpt4_bias_amplification: 2.8\n      qwen3_accuracy: 0.76\n      qwen3_delta_pi_max: 0.13\n      qwen3_bias_amplification: 3.6\n      claude_sonnet_accuracy: 0.79\n      claude_sonnet_delta_pi_max: 0.11\n      claude_sonnet_bias_amplification: 3.1\n      # --- EC-HTE benefit by LLM ---\n      echte_rmse_improvement_gpt4: 0.08        # modest improvement for best LLM\n      echte_rmse_improvement_claude: 0.11\n      echte_rmse_improvement_qwen3: 0.15       # largest improvement for noisiest LLM\n      # --- Correlation between LLM quality and EC-HTE benefit ---\n      correlation_accuracy_vs_echte_benefit: -0.92  # better LLM → less EC-HTE benefit\n      correlation_delta_pi_vs_echte_benefit: 0.88   # more heterogeneous → more benefit\n      # --- Ensemble analysis ---\n      ensemble_majority_vote_accuracy: 0.85\n      ensemble_delta_pi_max: 0.07              # ensemble reduces heterogeneity\n      ensemble_bias_amplification: 2.1         # but doesn't eliminate it\n    result_rationale: >\n      三个 LLM 的 accuracy 排序 GPT-4.1 > Claude Sonnet > Qwen3 反映了模型能力梯度。\n      关键发现是 Δπ（误分类异质性）与 overall accuracy 的关系并非单调——取决于每个 LLM\n      在哪些 subgroup 上 struggle。Claude Sonnet 的 accuracy 介于两者之间，但 Δπ=0.11\n      说明它的 errors 有不同的 subgroup pattern。\n\n      EC-HTE benefit 与 LLM quality 的高负相关（-0.92）是预期的：worse LLM → more heterogeneous\n      errors → more room for stratified correction to help。这支持 \"EC-HTE as insurance policy\"\n      的 narrative——特别是在使用 cheaper/faster 但 noisier LLMs 时。\n\n      Ensemble 分析显示 majority vote 提高 accuracy（0.85）但不消除 heterogeneity（Δπ=0.07，\n      amplification 2.1x），说明 \"just use ensemble\" 不是 EC-HTE 的替代品。\n      但 ensemble + EC-HTE 的 marginal benefit 可能很小，这是 honest limitation。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T13\"\n        caption: \"LLM annotator comparison: quality, heterogeneity, and EC-HTE benefit\"\n        columns: [\"LLM\", \"Accuracy\", \"Δπ_max\", \"Bias Amplification\", \"EC-HTE RMSE Gain\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4.1\", \"0.82\", \"0.09\", \"2.8\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"Claude Sonnet 4.6\", \"0.79\", \"0.11\", \"3.1\", \"0.11\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-235B\", \"0.76\", \"0.13\", \"3.6\", \"0.15\"]\n          - [\"Majority Vote Ensemble\", \"0.85\", \"0.07\", \"2.1\", \"0.05\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot of Δπ_max vs EC-HTE RMSE improvement, one point per LLM + ensemble. Clear positive trend. Could go to appendix.\"\n    analysis: >\n      P1 实验，适合 appendix。核心 message 简洁：EC-HTE 对 noisier annotators 更有价值。\n      Ensemble 不替代 EC-HTE 因为不消除 heterogeneity。三个 LLM 的 heterogeneity pattern\n      不同（different subgroups are hard for different LLMs），说明 one-size-fits-all\n      correction 本质不可行。\n\n  - name: \"Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      CATE-weighted adaptive allocation vs uniform vs uncertainty-only allocation.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Allocation strategies at n_expert=250 ---\n      rmse_uniform_allocation: 0.082\n      rmse_uncertainty_allocation: 0.075       # allocate more to high-uncertainty subgroups\n      rmse_cate_weighted_allocation: 0.071     # allocate more to high-CATE × high-error\n      rmse_oracle_allocation: 0.065\n      # --- Improvement over uniform ---\n      improvement_uncertainty_vs_uniform: 0.085  # 8.5% RMSE improvement\n      improvement_cate_weighted_vs_uniform: 0.134 # 13.4% improvement\n      # --- But gains are modest ---\n      improvement_cate_weighted_vs_uncertainty: 0.053  # only 5.3% beyond uncertainty-only\n      # --- Practical issue: needs pilot CATE estimates ---\n      pilot_fraction_needed: 0.15              # 15% of budget for pilot\n      pilot_quality_sensitivity: \"moderate\"     # noisy pilot → suboptimal allocation\n    result_rationale: >\n      Adaptive allocation 的改进存在但 modest（13.4% over uniform），因为 median 档下\n      subgroup 间的 CATE heterogeneity 较温和——如果 CATE 相差不大，把更多 labels 分给\n      high-CATE subgroups 的 marginal value 有限。CATE-weighted 比 uncertainty-only 仅多 5.3%，\n      因为 high-error subgroups（uncertainty-only targets）和 high-CATE subgroups 有较大 overlap\n      （LLM 在 harder subgroups 上通常 error 更高，而 harder subgroups 往往有 larger effects）。\n      Pilot fraction 15% 进一步 eats into available budget。P2 优先级合理——收入产出比有限。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T14\"\n        caption: \"Allocation strategy comparison (n_expert=250, K=4, extreme regime)\"\n        columns: [\"Strategy\", \"RMSE\", \"Improvement vs Uniform\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Uniform\", \"0.082\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Uncertainty-only\", \"0.075\", \"8.5%\"]\n          - [\"CATE-weighted\", \"0.071\", \"13.4%\"]\n          - [\"Oracle\", \"0.065\", \"20.7%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: RMSE vs allocation strategy bar chart. Diminishing returns visible from uniform → uncertainty → CATE-weighted → oracle.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix 级别结果。CATE-weighted allocation 有理论吸引力但实际改进有限，\n      且需要额外的 pilot phase。推荐在论文中作为 \"extension\" 简要提及，\n      detailed results in appendix。如果 page budget 紧张，可以完全省略。\n\n  - name: \"Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      Test EC-HTE when subgroups are noisy/overlapping or when the true subgroup structure\n      doesn't align with the conditioning variable.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Scenario 1: Noisy subgroup assignment (10% mislabeling) ---\n      echte_rmse_clean_subgroups: 0.072\n      echte_rmse_10pct_noise: 0.085            # 18% RMSE degradation\n      echte_rmse_20pct_noise: 0.105            # 46% degradation\n      echte_rmse_30pct_noise: 0.132            # approaches global correction level\n      # --- Scenario 2: True K=4 but model uses K=2 ---\n      echte_rmse_correct_K4: 0.082\n      echte_rmse_misspecified_K2: 0.098        # 20% degradation\n      echte_rmse_overspecified_K8: 0.095       # 16% degradation from small-sample variance\n      # --- Scenario 3: Continuous moderator discretized ---\n      echte_rmse_correct_discretization: 0.075\n      echte_rmse_coarse_discretization: 0.092  # lose granularity\n      echte_rmse_fine_discretization: 0.098    # too many subgroups, insufficient data\n      # --- HB vs MLE under misspecification ---\n      hb_degradation_10pct_noise: 0.15         # 15% RMSE increase\n      mle_degradation_10pct_noise: 0.25        # 25% RMSE increase — HB more robust\n      hb_degradation_misspecified_K: 0.18\n      mle_degradation_misspecified_K: 0.30\n      # --- \"Graceful degradation\" metric ---\n      echte_worse_than_no_correction_at_noise: 0.35  # EC-HTE becomes worse than no-correction at 35% subgroup noise\n      global_worse_than_no_correction_at_noise: 0.05  # global becomes worse at 5% error heterogeneity — much less robust\n    result_rationale: >\n      Robustness analysis 在 median 档下展示 \"graceful degradation\"——EC-HTE 在 misspecification\n      下性能降低但 gradually，不会 catastrophically fail 直到 noise 极高（35%）。\n      对比 global correction 在 5% heterogeneity 时就变 harmful，EC-HTE 的 robustness 优势明显。\n\n      10% subgroup noise 导致 18% RMSE degradation 的原因：noisy subgroup assignment\n      意味着混淆矩阵估计混合了来自错误 subgroup 的 labels，导致 per-subgroup correction\n      偏向 global（因为混合了多个 subgroup 的 signal）。HB 的 partial pooling 在这里帮助——\n      当 subgroup signal 被 noise 稀释时，HB 自动 shrink toward global，而 MLE 会 fit noise。\n      这是 HB \"never worse than global\" 性质的又一体现。\n\n      Misspecified K（真实 K=4，模型用 K=2）损失 20% 是因为 K=2 将两对不同的 subgroups\n      合并，部分丧失了 stratification 的精确性。但 K=2 仍远优于 global（0.098 vs ~0.19），\n      说明 even coarse stratification helps。Overspecified K=8 的 16% degradation\n      来自 small-sample variance（n/8 per subgroup），与 exp-006 的发现一致。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T15\"\n        caption: \"Robustness: EC-HTE RMSE under subgroup misspecification\"\n        columns: [\"Scenario\", \"Clean\", \"Mild Misspec.\", \"Moderate Misspec.\", \"Severe Misspec.\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Subgroup noise\", \"0.072 (0%)\", \"0.085 (10%)\", \"0.105 (20%)\", \"0.132 (30%)\"]\n          - [\"K misspecification\", \"0.082 (K=4)\", \"0.098 (K=2)\", \"0.095 (K=8)\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Discretization\", \"0.075 (correct)\", \"0.092 (coarse)\", \"0.098 (fine)\", \"—\"]\n      - table_id: \"T16\"\n        caption: \"HB vs MLE degradation under misspecification\"\n        columns: [\"Misspecification\", \"HB RMSE increase\", \"MLE RMSE increase\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"10% subgroup noise\", \"15%\", \"25%\"]\n          - [\"20% subgroup noise\", \"30%\", \"50%\"]\n          - [\"K=4→K=2\", \"18%\", \"30%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: RMSE vs subgroup noise level (0-40%), three lines: EC-HTE, global correction, no correction. Shows EC-HTE crossing no-correction at ~35% noise, global crossing at ~5% heterogeneity. Key message: EC-HTE degrades gracefully.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Robustness 是 median 档下补偿理论锐度不足的关键 empirical contribution。\n      \"EC-HTE is robust to 10-20% subgroup misspecification while global correction breaks at 5%\n      error heterogeneity\" 是有力的 practical message。HB 在 misspecification 下比 MLE 的优势\n      （15% vs 25% degradation）比在 correctly-specified 设定下更明显——\n      这支持 \"HB as robustness guarantee\" 的 narrative pivot。\n      建议将 Fig (RMSE vs noise) 放入 main paper 作为 robustness 的 key visualization。\n\n  - name: \"Causal Forest Integration\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      Apply EC-HTE post-hoc correction to CausalForestDML subgroup CATE estimates +\n      leaf-level corrected pseudo-outcomes with variance-adjusted CIs.\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Post-hoc correction of forest subgroup CATEs ---\n      cf_naive_subgroup_bias: 0.12\n      cf_global_corrected_subgroup_bias: 0.17  # global correction still hurts\n      cf_echte_corrected_subgroup_bias: 0.06\n      cf_oracle_corrected_subgroup_bias: 0.03\n      # --- Leaf-level correction ---\n      cf_leaf_naive_rmse: 0.22\n      cf_leaf_echte_rmse: 0.18                 # modest improvement at leaf level\n      cf_leaf_global_rmse: 0.26                # global hurts at leaf level too\n      # --- Variance-adjusted CIs ---\n      cf_echte_coverage_subgroup: 0.90\n      cf_echte_coverage_leaf: 0.87             # harder to cover at leaf level\n      cf_naive_coverage_subgroup: 0.82\n      cf_naive_coverage_leaf: 0.79\n      # --- Comparison with diff-in-means ---\n      dim_echte_rmse: 0.072                    # from exp-001\n      cf_echte_rmse: 0.065                     # CF slightly better due to flexibility\n      cf_advantage_over_dim: 0.10              # 10% RMSE improvement\n    result_rationale: >\n      Causal forest integration 在 median 档下显示 EC-HTE 的 correction 与 CATE estimator\n      choice 正交——bias mechanism 和 correction 适用于任何 estimator。Global correction\n      在 CF 输出上同样 harmful（0.17 vs naive 0.12），EC-HTE 同样 helpful（0.06）。\n\n      Leaf-level correction 比 subgroup-level improvement 更 modest（0.22→0.18 vs 0.12→0.06）\n      因为 leaves 的 granularity 超过 confusion matrix estimation 的 resolution——\n      一个 leaf 可能包含多个 subgroup 的混合，使得 subgroup-specific correction 只是 partial fix。\n      Coverage 在 leaf level 更差（87%）因为 leaf-level CATE variance 本身更大且 harder to estimate。\n\n      CF vs diff-in-means 的 10% advantage 说明 estimator choice matters but is secondary\n      to the correction method choice。论文 message：EC-HTE 是 estimator-agnostic 的 correction\n      layer。\n    tables:\n      - table_id: \"T17\"\n        caption: \"EC-HTE with CausalForestDML: subgroup and leaf-level results\"\n        columns: [\"Level\", \"Naive\", \"Global\", \"EC-HTE\", \"Oracle\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Subgroup CATE bias\", \"0.12\", \"0.17\", \"0.06\", \"0.03\"]\n          - [\"Subgroup coverage\", \"0.82\", \"0.75\", \"0.90\", \"0.94\"]\n          - [\"Leaf CATE RMSE\", \"0.22\", \"0.26\", \"0.18\", \"0.14\"]\n          - [\"Leaf coverage\", \"0.79\", \"0.72\", \"0.87\", \"0.93\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: CATE heterogeneity plot (forest-based) with and without EC-HTE correction. Shows correction preserving heterogeneity structure while reducing bias.\"\n    analysis: >\n      P1 实验，main paper 中简要展示 subgroup-level 结果即可。Leaf-level 分析可放 appendix。\n      核心 takeaway：EC-HTE is estimator-agnostic。CF 的 flexibility 提供 modest additional\n      improvement over diff-in-means，但不是论文的重点。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"bab92f78-da56-473f-9e96-ce17b8b932a9","total_cost_usd":0.5192985,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10224,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":17765,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10224,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":17765,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10224},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5198,"outputTokens":29,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0053430000000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":17765,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10224,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5139555,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"e0568863-dbba-4b92-abe1-a15118fe78ef"}
